, then once an opportunity opens up, he will strike using wasp sting blur.<br /> <br /> <br /> background-added if necessary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","user":"black orchid","date":".  forgot to add reasons :) 01-02-2014, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T03:52:41-08:00","id":41016,"title":"","content":"Hmm, a contribution based on a mechanical experiment is a bit outside of my comfort zone...<br /> <br /> I'll see what I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:12:28-08:00","id":41020,"title":"","content":"I'll give it a shot as well, but I have a feeling this is going to be difficult. At least, if they are intended to survive Exalt-level combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:30:23-08:00","id":41026,"title":"","content":"Will post something later today, not sure how combat capable they would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:43:25-08:00","id":41031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted#post40920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are interested in contributing to the good of Lunars in EX3, please aid us in an experiment.<br /> <br /> Make three 2.5 Lunar characters, one of each caste, with starting character creation rules. Make each caste compliment the other, with mostly different Charms. Make each caste perform to the typical role of its caste.<br /> <br /> Reply to this thread with each of your three sample Lunars's traits and Charms. Explain why you gave them the Charms you did, and how they compliment one another.<br /> <br /> I apologize but I am too busy to answer questions about this experiment. Just know that your participation will be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm...I'm going to echo Levi on that one, pretty much to the last word. But still, tis fun! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:48:03-08:00","id":41032,"title":"","content":"No Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Tyrant Lizard<br /> Strength 3 Dexterity 3 <b>Stamina 3</b><br /> Charisma 2 Manipulation 2 Appearance 3<br /> <b>Perception 5 Intelligence 5 Wits 3</b><br /> <br /> Favoured:<br /> Investigation 5 Survival 3<br /> Other:<br /> Awareness 3 Integrity 2 Investigation 3 (reading people +1) Larceny 2 (knowing the criminal mind +1) Martial Arts 3, Lore 3 (making deductions +1) Occult 3 Stealth 2 (crowds +1) Resistance 2<br /> <br /> Compassion 1 Conviction 3 Temperance 5 Valour 2<br /> Essence 2<br /> Willpower 10<br /> <br /> Knacks:<br /> Towering Beast Form<br /> Charms:<br /> Hide of the Cunning Hunter<br /> One of the Herd<br /> First Perception Excellency<br /> Eagle Eye Advantage<br /> Blood-Kin Sense<br /> Motive Dissecting Eye<br /> Leaf Falling Scrutiny<br /> First Intelligence Excellency<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<br /> Will be added as necessary<br /> <br /> While the Changing Moon is a stereotypical party face going after large social dice pools and the Full Moon will obviously be a fighter, the No Moon is intended to be the brains of the operation facilitating both roles with intel provided from Motive Dissecting Eye, Leaf Falling Scrutiny and Blood-Kin Sense.<br /> Can support the Full Moon in a fight by assuming the Tyrant Lizard shape and using Eagle Eye Advantage to get +6 dice from Aim actions. At high essence this may involve an Emperor Ox Tyrant Lizard being ridden into battle by a Deadly Beastman Transformation Full Moon in a manner reminiscent of the Ultrazord from Power Rangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:49:00-08:00","id":41033,"title":"","content":"I've been lurking for a while, and seeing this made me decide to register! So, here's my first one, the next two will be up shortly!<br /> <br /> Name: Totally Not Alex Mercer<br /> Caste: Full Moon<br /> Totem: Slime Mold<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 4*, Dexterity 5*, Stamina 3*, Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 4*, Perception 3<br /> Abilities: Martial Arts 5* (Natural Weapons +3), Athletics 3, Awareness 3, War 2, Investigation 3, Presence 3 (Pretending to be someone else +1), Socialize 3, Stealth 3, Survival 2*<br /> Virtues: Compassion 1, Temperance 1, Conviction 3, Valor 4<br /> Willpower: 10, Permanent Limit: 5<br /> Backgrounds: Backing (The Guild) 3, Contacts (The Guild, The Salinan Society, Mercenary Companies) 3, Reputation (Anti-Realm Terrorist) 1<br /> <br /> Knacks: Prey's Skin Disguise, Quicksilver Form, Body of Acid, Assimilation of Prey, Grotesque Pseudopodia, Defense of Meaningless Shape<br /> Charms: Claws of the Silver Moon, Armor-Forming Technique, Limb-Sheilding Growth, First Dexterity Excellency,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1878,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","user":"AdamantineRapier","date":". 01-02-2014, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:57:26-08:00","id":41039,"title":"","content":"I just wish we were allowed to use Peter Schaeffer's chargen, as it seems (from what I understand) to have been the original intent of how to make a Second Edition Lunar.<br /> <br /> Will post a trio later today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T05:19:51-08:00","id":41051,"title":"","content":"Name: Totally Not The Dude on a Manowar Cover<br /> Caste: Changing Moon<br /> Totem: A Polar Bear<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Charisma 5, Manipulation 2, Appearance 5, Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Perception 2<br /> Abilities: Athletics 3, Integrity 3, Martial Arts 5* (Brutal Force +1), War 3, Linguistics 3 (Native: Skytongue, Other: Old Realm, two others), Performance 5 (Singing +3), Presence 3, Socialize 2, Survival 2<br /> Virtues: Compassion 1, Temperance 1, Conviction 3, Valor 4<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Backgrounds: Artifact (Moonsilver Artifact Staff) 2, Allies (Half-naked spirit-women) 3, Followers (Nordic Warriors) 2<br /> <br /> Knacks: Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> Charms: First Charisma Excellency, Third Appearance Excellency, Perfect Symmetry, New Friend Aroma, Terrifying Lust Infliction<br /> Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style: Inspiring Battle Hymn, Terrifying Battle Shriek","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1878,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","user":"AdamantineRapier","date":". 01-02-2014, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T05:35:10-08:00","id":41053,"title":"","content":"Name: Something Actually Original This Time, Really<br /> Caste: No Moon<br /> Totem: Owl<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 5*, Stamina 2, Charisma 3, Manipulation 1, Appearance 3, Intelligence 4*, Wits 4*, Perception 4*<br /> Abilities: Awareness 3, Integrity 3, Martial Arts 2, Melee 3 (Spear and Shield +1), War 3, Lore 3, Occult 5 (Demons +3)*, Presence 3, Survival 2*<br /> Virtues: Compassion 1, Temperance 3, Conviction 4, Valor 1<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Backgrounds: Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Direlance), Artifact 2 (Sentinel Defense Force Bracers), Manse 3 (Key of Mastery/Gem of Sorcery)<br /> <br /> Knacks: Hybrid Body Rearrangement<br /> Charms: First Dexterity Excellency, Terrestrial Circle Initiation<br /> Spells: Demon of the First Circle, Emerald Circle Banishment, Emerald Circle Countermagic, Open the Spirit Door, Stormwind Rider","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1878,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","user":"AdamantineRapier","date":". 01-02-2014, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T05:44:32-08:00","id":41058,"title":"","content":"People do remember that they have to explain why they build these character's that way, right?<br /> <br /> Because only 1 or two people have...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  errors...I do corrcet them when I have time...or intrest 01-03-2014, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:01:43-08:00","id":41060,"title":"","content":"<b>Introduction: A small circle of three Lunars serving MaHa is his wars against eastern powers. They have all the tools they need to wage guerrilla warfare, collect information of enemy movements, infiltrate cities, gather spirit allies and so on.</b><br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Full Moon: [Stam &amp; Charisma]</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://img827.imageshack.us/img827/5084/jljv.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> Basic Idea: The face of the Circle (though the New Moon is a good wing man) \u2013 the Full Moon keeps the New Moon alive, his troops alive and can act as Yojimbo. While his charms are focused on being a sponge \u2013 his abilities are focused on being a consummate statesman and keeping the camp fed and in line. <div align=\"center\">Charms:<br /> Hard Mode: No DBT</div> <br /> <br /> Stamina Excel (second)<br /> Armor Forming Technique \u2013 Damage Mitigation<br /> Limb Shielding Growth \u2013 Damage Mitigation<br /> Mother Grizzly Attitude \u2013 Hard lock against spell disruption<br /> Bruise Relief \u2013 Speed Bump<br /> Halting the Scarlet Flow \u2013 Bodyguard for days<br /> Snarling Watchdog Retribution \u2013 Mostly to fuel Scarlet Flow in absence of DBT.<br /> Charisma Excel (First)<br /> Maintaining the Pack \u2013 Ablative armor regeneration <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>New Moon: [Charisma &amp; Intelligence]<br /> <img src=\"http://img853.imageshack.us/img853/3712/7pnl.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></b></div> <br /> <br /> Basic Idea: The New Moon is tied to the Full Moon very closely in this circle. He trains the men (lol, no, animals mostly) and even recruits them. He is able to set the Changing moon up with a lot of opportunities to ply his trade with tricks of the trade \u2013 acting as his wing man. Without the New Moon the other two would be not even half as effective. This guy is a force multiplier on so many levels.<br /> <br /> Synergy: The lack of Beast Form on the Full Moon in order to allow defensive actions such as body guarding lends itself to the need for a respite for powering up. <div align=\"center\"><br /> Charms:</div> <br /> <br /> Charisma Excel (First)<br /> Dog-Tongue Method \u2013 Mostly a speed bump charm to the impressive animal training charm. Animal intelligence being what it is a ST can easily make this charm worthless or godly (ex: cephalopods have terrible memory and forget what they were just doing after only a few seconds - making them worthless for the purpose of gathering information) further many ST\u2019s do not know much about animal behavior.<br /> Nature-Reinforcing Allocation \u2013 Fixes the above issue of animal intelligence and opens up the tool box that is the mutation system. Given allies, friendships and familiars \u2013 this can provide the Circle a great deal of flexible power in terms of: brute strength, spy network, rudimentary construction and resource gathering.<br /> Wolf Pack Training Technique - Training the elites<br /> Cobra Hypnotic Method \u2013 Social surgical strike to remove influence of enemy factions or simply roadblocks \u2013 also allows you to set up deathblows for the other two in the Circle.<br /> Perfect Fear Scent \u2013 Combos with Wasp Dance nicely and could be used as a moral hit in mass battle or as part of a terror campaign (in or out of your own community \u2013 control) therefore hitting Social/Martial and Social all at once.<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery:<br /> Impenetrable Frost Barrier \u2013 Suppress Withering Fire<br /> Impervious Sphere of Water \u2013 Everything the Full Moon needs to power up.<br /> Commanding the Beasts \u2013 Turn any battle into a mass battle, send a tide of rats and alley toms to disrupt a chase, used to build long term army and play off Nature Reinforcing or even steal a town blind (with intelligent rat thieves). <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Changing Moon or Full Moon: [Dex, Stam]</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://img842.imageshack.us/img842/1830/3ze1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> Basic Idea: This Lunar is the eyes of the circle and ghosts into locations to kidnap or spy. He is also counter ops, being able to sniff out enemy spies and even spirits. Finally the Lunar is the hammer to this \u2018Anvil and Hammer\u2019 Circle - sneaking about the edges of the combat lobbing stones with explosive power. Between supernal smell and the ability to see immaterial \u2013 nothing should sneak up on them and mundane closing actions are foolish against the Lunar\u2019s speed. Further, having only essence 2 allows for a lot of room to spend BP on artifacts/contacts/charms and so on. <div align=\"center\">Charms:</div> <br /> <br /> Perception Excel (Second)<br /> Inevitable Spoor Discovery \u2013 Most stealth charms seem to diminish sound and sight but leaves smell wide open. This charm is useful for sweeping the perimeter of an armed camp, smelling out the guard rotation of enemy camps, faultless tracking and other cleverness. Being able to identify beasts also allows one to locate potential targets for the New Moon to bind pact with.<br /> Eagle Eye Advantage \u2013 While the New Moon and Full Moon act as the anvil and herd in mass combat \u2013 this charm allows the stealthy Changing Moon to murder face hard.<br /> Wolf Eye Advantage \u2013 Shrugging off drugs (dulled senses) is useful for a changing moon \u2013 like the Vizzini scene from Princess Bride. Seeing through fog and foliage is a great boon to the above.<br /> Eye of the Cat \u2013 See what you\u2019re really getting into. Attacking a sorcerer with a score of dematerialized Demons is a sad way to die. And yes, ST\u2019s should have sorcerers be intelligent and kill you that way.<br /> Dex Excel (First)<br /> Instinct \u2013 Driven Beast Movement \u2013 Kite and find new sniper nests<br /> Impressions of Strength(Ogre\u2019s Loving Caress) \u2013 Artifact sling with piercing and high strength will roll tons of dice.<br /> Shell-Crushing Atemi \u2013 Artifact Sling picks up piercing (welcome to exit wounds)<br /> DBT and tons of camouflage mutations\u2026cause I\u2019ve never seen a Lunar stealth charm (like one you could use in combat) outside of customs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 01-02-2014, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:40:11-08:00","id":41072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>black orchid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41015#post41015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yay lunars, I love those guys!, and Id love to help, here's my first attempt, hope it helps, ill post the other two when I get time later<br /> <br /> name-auspicious foreboding dog<br /> concept- beast master<br /> Caste- changing moon<br /> motivation- defend his homeland from the foreign invaders<br /> Attribute<br /> strength 2, dexterity 3, stamina 2<br /> charisma 5, manipulation 3, appearance 3<br /> intelligence 3, wits 3, perception 4<br /> skills<br /> melee 3(attacking from surprise, presence 2(talking to his nationality+1), stealth 3, survival 3(hunting+1), resistance 2, lore 1, craft 2(wood)(traps+1), ride 3, performance 2, awareness 3, dodge 2<br /> compassion 3, valor 2, conviction 3, temperance 2<br /> Essence 3<br /> Willpower 7<br /> background<br /> familiar 2<br /> familiar 2<br /> artifact 2<br /> resources 1<br /> contacts 1<br /> influence 1<br /> charms<br /> 1st charisma excellency<br /> dog tongue method<br /> nature-reinforcing allocation<br /> boundary-marking meditation<br /> 2nd wits excellency<br /> wasp sting blur<br /> 1st perception excellency<br /> eagle eye advantage<br /> life of the hummingbird<br /> <br /> reasons for charms- most are used to train/raise animals, in combat ending combat fast is this characters way of fighting, using his animals to make an opening, he has his own territory and proudly defends it, and his Excellency's are just there to boost him up in a challenge.<br /> <br /> using his allies/pets, he will take a aim action(boosted by the eagle eye method, then once an opportunity opens up, he will strike using wasp sting blur.<br /> <br /> <br /> background-added if necessary</div> </div> </div> </div>here's number 2(in my honest opinion not that great) ~name-harbinger of the waves<br /> concept- pirate hunter<br /> Caste- no moon<br /> motivation- destroy the coral pirate allies<br /> spirit shape- sea dragon<br /> Attribute<br /> strength 4, dexterity 2, stamina 4<br /> charisma 3, manipulation 3, appearance 1<br /> intelligence 3, wits 4, perception 5<br /> skills<br /> brawl 2, presence 2, stealth , survival 3, resistance 2(holding breath+1), lore 3, craft , sail 1, performance 2(threats+1), athletics 4(feats of strength+2), occult 2, investigation 1, medicine 2, dodge 3<br /> compassion 1, valor 3, conviction 3, temperance 2<br /> Essence 3<br /> Willpower 7<br /> backgrounds<br /> hearts blood 3<br /> contacts 1<br /> artifact 3<br /> charms/knacks<br /> 1st wits excellency<br /> 3rd perception excellency<br /> towering beast form<br /> mountainous spirit expression<br /> Wyld sensing instincts<br /> wasp sting blur<br /> many armed monkey<br /> meerkat alertness<br /> ox body technique<br /> charms reasons- relying on brute force of his spirit shape and his sharp wit of his mind to land a devastating arrays of blows.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:43:49-08:00","id":41076,"title":"","content":"If you use dropbox you could always put them in the public folder in dropbox and post a link to them. Just right click on the file when it is in the public folder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:58:14-08:00","id":41081,"title":"","content":"Full Moon - He who fights men<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div sty