000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf\u25cf,</span></span></span> Contacts (typically spirits in local courts) <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span>, Manse <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Knacks: Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> <br /> Charms: First Strength Ex, Second Dex Ex, First Perception Ex, Eye of the Cat, Devil-Restraining Grip, God-Cutting Essence, Righteous Lion Defense<br /> <br /> Whys and whyfors:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The wandering exorcist who protects mortals from the ravages of unscrupulous gods and demons. You are a specialist in fighting those which evade the notice of mortals. From this point forward your progression moves very much like a Full Moon's, although you'll obviously be slower to achieve your ultimate martial prowess than the Full Moon, but the trade-off is obvious. This is the kind of character that a campaign has to work around, of course, which means you probably need to make sure this is going to be okay with your Storyteller and warn the other players that a significant amount of encounters will be with things they can't hurt through normal means. At least until their exorcist gets a hand on them and drags them kicking and screaming into material form, anyway.</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> So you've probably picked up on a few recurring themes in chargen. I'll address all of them here:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Why Athletics, Awareness, Dodge, Integrity, and Martial Arts for every character? Also, why is Martial Arts always favored? Because these are your basic &quot;being Exalted and not immediately dying&quot; Abilities. You need to them to get 2-die stunts consistently and not get wrecked in combat, physical or social. Martial Arts is always favored because Martial Arts are such a huge Charm investment that not making them favored using the standard rules is like shooting yourself in the face to avoid shooting yourself in the foot later. Also Martial Arts controls using your natural weapons in your non-human forms, should you have any, which makes it a good investment period.<br /> <br /> You don't pick up Perfect Defenses. Why? Because in 2.5e if your Storyteller expects you to be able to survive paranoia combat out of chargen, you should be looking for another game, not building a character whose only trick is Flowing Body Evasion and the defense-enhancement Dexterity Charms on the way there. Honestly, it shouldn't even be on your &quot;want&quot; radar until around E4 when you're likely to face opponents with perfect attacks. Particularly as a Lunar the best investment is probably soak Charms/armor and Ox-Bodies instead of the entire Dex dodge tree.<br /> <br /> You're deep in Willpower investment out of the gate. Why? Because Lunars need to use Willpower to be able to get more than 5 dice enhancing their actions. Stupid but true.<br /> <br /> Dex 5 and Second Dex Excellency? Spend four motes to get DV buff. A no-brainer since you'll stunt those motes right back.<br /> <br /> You sure like Manses. Why? Because not taking Manse 2 and a hearthstone at chargen is hard mode. Lunars are premised on the idea that they have lairs to crawl back to. Have a lair. Get free motes.<br /> <br /> How can you have a Lunar with no Heart's Blood!? Easy. Don't worry about shape-shifting except to DBT because you probably won't. If you do, it won't be for long since you can't maintain a non-native form while expending motes. Crappy answer, isn't it? Welcome to Lunars.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I didn't address any questions, feel free to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T07:26:27-08:00","id":41099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41039#post41039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish we were allowed to use Peter Schaeffer's chargen, as it seems (from what I understand) to have been the original intent of how to make a Second Edition Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Schaefer's chargen results in much more interesting and versatile characters, yes. But it doesn't come close to addressing the real problems that undermine how Lunars operate by comparison to Sidereals and Solars. A lot of house rules go into good Lunar characters. A lot of custom Charms, too. But I'll freely admit you can make good and interesting Lunars right out of chargen in 2.5e if you've got a Storyteller who's willing to work with you and even a couple that don't require your ST to work with you. Although they may flip out when you start using Charms that should have been errata'd out but didn't quite get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T07:47:15-08:00","id":41110,"title":"","content":"Because Lunars are not my forte, I took a while building these, yet they are still <b>far</b> from &quot;optimized.&quot; <br /> <br /> <i>Notes will be italicized</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Spider-Men!</b><br /> Full Moon First!<br /> <b>Warrior Spider</b><br /> Spirit Shape: Giant Spider<br /> <i>Naturally. Gotta go with the biggest spider for the physical guy! This is gonna be easy!</i><br /> Tell: Coarse, bristly &quot;fur.&quot;<br /> <i>Going good so far! He's gonna be the muscle, while New and Changing can handle spirits and the social arenas respectively!</i><br /> Attributes: Str 4 (C), Dex 5 (C), Sta 3 (C)<br /> <i>Figure he's a big strong guy, but also nimble. He should land terrifying flurries in his Beastman form!</i><br /> Cha 3, Man 3, App 1.<br /> [i]Big guy ain't very social, so I'll make it his tertiary. I want him to be <b>one ugly mofo,</b> so I'm gonna put his Appearance at 1\u2026 with the unintended side-effect of making him actually above-average in Charisma and Manipulation. Sure, let's go with that.<br /> Per 3, Int 2, Wits 4<br /> [i]Wits is used for JB and not much else for a combat character. I don't want him to be blind or rock-stupid, so I'll make mental his secondary.<br /> Abilities: Martial Arts 5 (Unarmed +2) (F) <i>whoo-hoo, this is gonna be a lot scarier when he pops Claws of the Silver Moon!</i>, Thrown 2 <i>backup resort</i>, Integrity 3 <i>As strong as he is, don't want him unexpectedly turning on his allies</i>, Presence 3 (Terror +2) <i>so ugly he's <b>scary</b></i>, Resistance 3 <i>Gotta stand and take a hit every now and again</i>, Survival 3 (F) <i>it's mandatory, but I'm okay with it for this guy - he'll be that much scarier when you can't hide from him!</i>, Investigation 3 <i>Spiders have Investigation in the Core book, why not?</i>, Athletics 3 <i>he's a jumping spider!</i>, Awareness 3 <i>JB rolls, all good here\u2026 and\u2026 done!</i><br /> Backgrounds: Artifact 3 (Moonsilver Superheavy Full Plate) <i>Wait, the Moonsilver SHFP's been errata'ed to change like the Moon-Faced Mail SHFP, and I get the Hardness still, for only two dots more? Sign me up!</i>, Manse 3 (Snakeskin Stone) <i>Wait, I get <b>how many</b> Charms? I won't be able to afford the super-healing! Better snag a hearthstone for quick recovery\u2026</i>, Tattoo Artifact 1 (Moonsilver Hearthstone Amulet) <i>gotta hold the stone to my skin somehow\u2026 no Heart's Blood for this guy, at least not yet. He's got all the shapes he needs right here\u2026</i><br /> Knacks: <i>Wait, I draw Knacks and Charms from the same pool? i better just get the one, then!</i> Deadly Beastman Transformation (Mutations: Extra Arms, Fur)<br /> Charms: <i>Seven Charms to do some Lunar-y stuff with\u2026 four of 'em have to be Caste/Favored? Like I was gonna pick any other kinds\u2026</i> Second Strength Excellency, First Dexterity Excellency [i]bread and butter, these two - prerequisites for <b>everything!</b>, Agitation of the Swarm Technique <i>He's gonna be scary in flurries!</i>, Wasp Sting Blur <i>not too bad, kinda speedbump-y</i>, Octopus and Spider Barrage<i> looks like scary flurries are gonna be pretty much all he does for a while\u2026</i>, Relentless Lunar Fury <i>what Lunar combatant is complete without you?</i><br /> Virtues: Compassion 1, Conviction 5 (Virtue Flaw: Curse of the Hungry Wolverine), Temperance 2, Valor 3 <i>Seems about right\u2026 as a plus, the high Conviction gives me a <b>lot</b> of motes!</i><br /> Willpower: 8, Essence 3 <i>Gotta get the 3 if you wanna do anything</i><br /> <br /> Let's go with the No Moon next!<br /> <b>Shaman Spider</b><br /> Spirit Shape: <i>Wait, I'm allowed a form <b>how</b> small, without Knacks? Crap, I gotta buy a Knack just so they're not <b>both</b> giant spiders.</i> Some kind of spider that's bigger than a mouse, but smaller than a cat. Hell if I know.<br /> Tell: Unusually shiny eyes. <i>I like this one. Off to a rocky start, but that was pretty nice.</i><br /> Attributes: <i>Hoo, boy. I have <b>no idea</b> what I need. For now I'll prioritize mental and see what happens.</i> <br /> Str 1, Dex 5 (F), Sta 3 <i>He's a puny, wrinkled thing, but he's tough, and got the moves of a man half his age.</i><br /> Cha 3, Man 2, App 2 <i>Nothing exceptional to see here, let's move on\u2026</i><br /> Per 4 (C), Int 4 (C), Wits 3 (C) <i>We'll see what these get me\u2026</i><br /> Abilities: <i>When in doubt, go with something Twilight-ish</i> Melee 2, Thrown 1 <i>He can use a sword or throw a knife, but it's not gonna be his primary thing</i>, Integrity 1, Performance 3 (Prayer +2) <i>Gotta get the attention of those spirits!</i>, Survival 2 (F) <i>Annoys me that in addition to being required to favor it, I've gotta put at least two dots into it to be a proper Lunar\u2026</i>, Craft (Wood) 1 <i>does some whittling in his downtime</i>, Lore 2 <i>do as the Twilight does</i>, Medicine 2 <i>setting broken bones is okay</i>, Occult 3 (F) <i>would raise it higher, but the &quot;can raise above 3 without BP&quot; errata clause didn't apply to Lunars, grumble grumble</i>, Awareness 3, Dodge 2, Stealth 2, Linguistics 1 <i>knowing Old Realm is practically a necessity when you're dealing with spirits and crap!</i><br /> Backgrounds: <i>Gonna need Resources if I wanna do thaumaturgy stuff, or bribe spirits or whatever. I think I'll go with some Heart's Blood this time 'round, too, save me some Charms so I don't have to get travel spells\u2026</i> Artifact 1 (Moonsilver Hearthstone Amulet), Heart's Blood 1 (Forms: Hawk, Horse, Dog), Manse 3 (Gem of Sorcery), Resources 3<br /> Knacks: Humble Mouse Shape <i>why do I need minimum Stamina 3 to turn into something tiny, and an even higher Stamina to turn into something smaller still? Eh, I'll just backwards-justify it as him being a larger spider and being kinda tough or something\u2026</i><br /> Charms: <i>Good Lord, why so many prerequisites? I've got no room for half the stuff I want!</i> Second Perception Excellency <i>speedbump</i>, Eye of the Cat <i>speedbump, <b>and</b> a Charm I hate</i>, Devil-Restraining Grip <i>a proper shaman Charm, it just cost me half my Charms to get it!</i>, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery <i>\u2026and there go the rest of them!</i><br /> Spells: Summon Demon, Summon Elemental, Death of Obsidian Butterflies <i>ahh, the classics\u2026</i><br /> Virtues: Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Temperance 5, Valor 2 <i>that extra Essence was just too tempting</i><br /> Willpower: 10, Essence: 3 <i>leaving me no points for the thaumaturgy stuff I wanted to do. I never make a good thaumaturgy character\u2026</i><br /> Well, that felt like a failure. Let's try the Changing Moon, shall we?<br /> <b>Trickster Spider</b> <i>right from the start, getting an Anansi feel from this guy. Let's see what I can do\u2026</i><br /> Spirit Shape: Why, a harmless little spider, of course! <i>Yeah, the size of a goddamned dinner plate; I'm <b>not</b> paying for Emerald Grasshopper Form!</i><br /> Tell: A lilting, musical quality to his voice. <i>1e Tells for the win!</i><br /> Attributes: <i>I want some combat capability, so I'm gonna favor Dex for this guy, too, but to make room I'll have to make mental his tertiary\u2026 that won't hurt me, right? Oh, god, I just looked at the Charms section - BUY WITS BUY WITS BUY WITS\u2026</i> Str 2, Dex 4 (F), Sta 3<br /> Cha 3 (C), Man 4 (C), App 4 (C)<br /> Per 2, Int 2, Wits 3 [i]you didn't buy enough, idiot.<br /> Abilities: Martial Arts 2, Integrity 1, Performance 5 (Storytelling +3) (F), Presence 3, Survival 2 (F)<i> grr\u2026</i>, Investigation 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Dodge 3, Larceny 3, Stealth 3, Bureaucracy 1, Linguistics 1, Socialize 3 (Fast-Talk +3) <i>Not as clean or economical as a Solar could've been, but still feels pretty trickster-ish. I feel good!</i><br /> Backgrounds: <i>And there it goes again. Some of the cleverest shapeshifter stuff can be done with just artifacts and hearthstones. I'll grab some Heart's Blood and try <b>not</b> to get a Mask, but I don't have the wiggle room to get any Knacks I'd want\u2026</i> Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Hearthstone Bracers), Artifact 2 (Unsurpassed Sanxian), Artifact 1 (Moonsilver Hearthstone Amulet), Contacts 2, Heart's Blood 2 (Will pick out forms later maybe), Manse 3 (Stone of Gender Transformation), Manse 2 (Chameleon Stone), Resources 3 <i>honestly kinda embarrassed that I spent so much on Backgrounds to be a good shapechanger, but it would have cost <b>more</b> if I'd bought those capabilities with Lunar Knacks!</i><br /> Knacks: Humble Mouse Shape <i>Still not gonna go with Emerald Grasshopper Form just so I can be tiny.</i><br /> Charms: <i>Crap, everything I want is locked behind Excellencies. <b>everything</b>. Wait, here's an Appearance Charm that seems nice, is rather trickster-ish, and has <b>no</b> prerequisites! Y'know what? I'm gonna see if I can do this without raising my Essence. Gotta save all those points for Backgrounds anyway\u2026</i> First Dexterity Excellency, First Charisma Excellency, Dog-Tongue Method <i>the clause about treating it like two separate Charms rankles me; what right-minded player is gonna have a Charisma or Perception of 1 and want to buy this Charm anyway? Still, Anansi talked to a lot of animals, let's get it\u2026</i>, Second Manipulation Excellency, Mirror Sight Dismay, Mask of White Jade, New Friend Aroma<br /> Virtues: Compassion 2, Conviction 3, Temperance 2, Valor 2 <i>Nothin' to see here, just didn't want another 5 after the last two.</i><br /> Willpower: 7, Essence: 2<br /> <br /> Okay, John, what can I say from here? At the first I tried to set 'em up to complement each other, but really I never felt I had the points to do it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:10:00-08:00","id":41120,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Here's a trio of Eastern Lunars fitting a wandering heros/anti-Realm saboteurs archetype. Note that they are very much unoptimized. Do tell if that's a problem for the purposes of this exercise.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Full Moon: the Warrior</b></span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Name: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sheep\u2019s Clothing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Spirit Shape: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Buffalo</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Motivation:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Break the control the Realm holds over Eastern territories</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence 2,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perception 3, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Wits 4</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Abilities:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> Athletics 5 (Feats of Strength +3)</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Awareness 3, Integrity 1, Melee 4 (Improvised Weapons +2),