"> 8</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Virtues: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Valor 1, Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Temperance 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">BP log:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-10: Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-3: WP 6-8</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2: Occult 4-5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-3: Contact 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lass has three roles: guide, medium and support. In human-populated areas, she hides as a cricket on Sheep\u2019s Clothing; in wild areas, she serves as a guide and can help avoid (or find) Wyld zones. She is the go-between of her circle when dealing with spirits, and has standing contracts with a few elementals whom she is allowed to summon without repercussion (as long as she doesn\u2019t bind them). In a fight, she offers her group the Frost Barrier\u2019s protection, then uses her Key of Mastery and anima power to blast their enemies with obsidian butterflies while relying on her dodging skills and small size to survive. In addition, she provides a Manse for the rest of the circle to go back to and hide/rest when needed.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Changing Moon: the Trickster</b></span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Name: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Circea</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Spirit Shape: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Peacock</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Motivation: </b>Ensure the coming of a society where she can be openly, gloriously obvious in her Lunar nature.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 2 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Charisma 5, Manipulation 4, Appearance 5</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence 2, Perception 3, Wits 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Abilities:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Melee 3 (Unexpected Attacks +1) Dodge 2, Larceny 3 (Disguise +1), Linguistics 3 (Rivertongue, Low Realm), Performance (Dance +1) 4, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Presence (Seduction +1) 5,</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Socialize 4, Lore 2, Bureaucracy 2, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Survival 1 </i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Knacks:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Prey Skin\u2019s Disguise, Changing Plumage Mastery</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Charms: </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Charisma:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> First Charisma Excellency, Cobra Hypnotic Method, Forgetful Victim Prana, Unnoticed Confusion Attack </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Manipulation:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> First Manipulation Excellency, Cat-Faced Presentation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Appearance: </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hide of the Cunning Hunter</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Backgrounds: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heart\u2019s Blood 3, Contacts 3 (Eastern Satrapies, Silver Pact, Linowan), Resources 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Essence:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Willpower:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Virtues: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Valor 2, Compassion 2, Conviction 3, Temperance 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">BP log:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2: Presence 4-5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2: Performance 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2: Socialize 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-5: Hide of the Cunning Hunter </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-3: Charisma 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-2: Willpower 6-7<br /> -2: Resources 1-3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Circea is an infiltrator and assassin. With her social Charms, she can blank out people\u2019s memories, lull people into a moment of Inactive weakness, slit their throats and disappear. There are fools everywhere who trust her, and she uses them gladly. As a maid or other unconspicious servant, she introduces thoughts, beliefs and Intimacies into people\u2019s heads without them ever noticing she did so (with Unnoticed Confusion Attack). Unexpected social attacks are absurdly punishing, so she uses that, too. When tagging along with Sheep\u2019s Clothing, she pretends to be an ordinary mortal companion who profits from his slow wits and lets other people in on the joke, drawing attention to herself and away from him. She is also the only one whose official identity can justify a certain amount of wealth, and as such is the one who provides the others with amenities and simple comfort when in urban settings.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-02-2014, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:48:54-08:00","id":41135,"title":"","content":"I love few things more than makin' up characters. I figured I'd make a set of three, a Lunar pack who work together with each other, shoring up each other's weaknesses and acting out the role of their caste within their group. I put 'em all on a boat together, named the boat the Gosling, and decided they were smugglers/pirates/messengers for older Lunars who weren't as mobile. I always start character gen by drawing a picture and then deciding what sorta character the person in my doodle is, so that's what the links on the names are (hey, it looks like you're looking at people's chargen processes, so I'm sharing my whole process). So here they are:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flyingspiderstudios.deviantart.com/art/Nergui-and-Gray-424069965\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Nergui: Changing Moon (Changing Moon, Sea Leopard Totem)</b></a><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Concept</b>: Seductive Selkie, Exiled Loner, Badass Whaler/Fisherman exiled from his homeland (and Exalted) for murdering a man who deserved murdering. This guy's a Strong Silent Type, which is a bit odd for a Changing Moon, but that's why I took Glance Oration Technique. Nergui (not his real name-it means &quot;No Name,&quot; for he is a broody exile) loves his loyal dog, fishing, and watching the night sky. He's a high-compassion high-temperance type who's got a soft spot for women and children that gets him into lots of trouble, because he lives on a boat and he always ends up trying to solve the problems of people he meets on shore before the Gosling ships out. If playing Nergui, I want to keep in mind the things that attracted me to the Sea Leopard as his Totem: he's a deadly lone hunter who's all about endurance and stamina rather than grace, he's playful even in combat, and he's got Selkie mojo which means he's always accidentally falling into tragic romance and then leaving for the sea. He's not a roguish chatterbox like so many Changing Moons, he's just smooth and sincere and easy to fall in love with.<br /> <br /> <b>Role In The Circle:</b> Nergui puts on false faces, using his Anima and Hide of the Cunning Hunter to act as an information-gatherer in new ports. Sometimes he flies ahead of the ship and determines what goods a town is in desperate need of so he can come back and tell Tu Nung what cargo to forge. He tends to grease the palms and deal with authorities when needed, because he smells friendly and he's the most physically attractive person on board. In ship-to-ship combat he's decent enough with his wavecleaver and his huge pet dog does a good job tripping up the enemy and ripping out jugulars. He's a bit of a tank: slow and solid and possessed of a strength Excellency, he uses Butterfly Eyes Defense and Glance Oration Technique in combat to try to scare powerful foes into thinking they're dealing with someone much more skilled than he actually is. He'll occasionally turn into his seal-form to smash into a ship from underneath. Usually, though, he bribes a flock of gulls to patrol the waters for miles around the ship and let him know if there's any other ships out there. They come in handy for avoiding the Realm navy and spotting fat merchant ships. Also? Nobody in this fucking party too ANY dots in Linguistics, so his use of Glance Oration Technique pretty much makes him the de facto translator when the ship inevitable sails to someplace that doesn't speak Firetongue or Riverspeak.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Str 3 Dex 2 Stam(F) 5, Cha 4 Man 3 App 4, Int 2 Per 2 Wit 3<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Sail(F) 3 (+1 Avoiding Sharp Rocks And Ice, +1 Night Sailing), Survival (F) 3 (+1 Cold Climates, +1 Animal Training), Athletics 3, Melee 3 (+1 Boarding Action), Socialize 2, Performance 2, Presence 3, Martial Arts 2, Integrity 1, Thrown 1 (+1 Harpoons), Larceny 2<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Familiar 2: (Gray, Badass Puppy), Artifact 2: (Wavecleaver), Hearts Blood 2: (Penguins, Fish, Birds), Contacts 1: Northern Sailors<br /> <b>Charms+Knacks:</b><br /> -1st Appearance Ex<br /> -Hide of the Cunning Hunter<br /> -New Friend Aroma<br /> -Glance Oration Technique<br /> -1st Manip Ex<br /> -Butterfly Eyes Defense<br /> -1st Str Ex<br /> -1st Cha Ex<br /> -Dog-Tongue Method<br /> -Nature Reinforcing Allocation<br /> <b>BP Spent On:</b> Essence 3, 2 Favored Charms, 2 Favored Specialties<br /> <b>Some Notes On Building This Character:</b> I kinda wanted room for some more social defensive charms. I want Nergui to be the quietly heroic type, and that means not being easily persuaded to betray his ideals. I'd also have loved a few more understated distraction-based charms, and it'd be nice to have room for some terrifying God-Seal-Beast charms for smashing up through ships, but for now he'll rely on the Strengthellency for that sorta thing. Goal here was to build a character who was less mind-screwy and more &quot;I'm just really likeable&quot;, so that's what I focused on in social charms. Bought Butterfly Eyes defense because I couldn't afford a Stam Excellency and a Stam defensive charm without losing my ability to buff my puppy, which was important to me because if puppies die it is sad. I wanted to take some Holy charms for this guy to represent his exiled wanderings in the north and fighting off Winter Folk, but there was no space. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flyingspiderstudios.deviantart.com/art/Spring-Rain-424069843\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Spring Rain: Full Moon (Full Moon, Osprey Totem)</b></a><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Concept:</b> Defender of the Downtrodden, Former Slave, Eye In The Sky, Rebel Leader. Spring Rain was a Bride of Ahlat (maybe in training? Her stats don't indicate the specialization of a Legion-of-Silence level combatant, which I think is what they're gonna look like in 3E) who was injured in battle, captured, and subsequently sold into slavery in the River Lands. She overcame her heroin addiction and led a slave revolt before escaping. Tu Nung found her and persuaded her to join his crew, and under her direction the Gosling has turned pirate and refugee-smuggler instead of just smuggling like it used to be. Spring Rain's a bit of an abolitionist and she's cost Tu Nung a lot of money by refusing to smuggle drugs, but piracy on Guild vessels has more than made up for it. She's getting dreams of building a navy out of freed slaves and creating a migratory ocean-going nation like the Denzik only with more pillaging of coastal regions, but her plans are still hazy. When playing Rain, I want to keep in mind the things that drew me to an Osprey as her totem: the myth from Ospreys are so majestic that fish turn belly-up in surrender, the story that Osprey parents have their children fly to the sun, and leave the ones that don't make it do die, and the fact that Ospreys are highly adaptable and migratory.<br /> <br /> <b>Role In The Circle: </b> Rain's got the Conviction in this party, and since her circlemates are both a bit shiftless she'll probably drive them in the direction of the plot. She's also the fighty one. She's by no means a death machine compared to other exalts, but she's fond of using Face of the Moon Concealment on the crew while pretending to be a merchant vessel prior to acts of piracy, and she's really good at grabbing people and throwing them overboard (where Nergui is sometimes waiting, depending on the engagement). Rain's charms are primarily built around combat, but she can also turn into a bird capable of flying 200 miles in a day (seriously, check Wikipedia!), which makes her the most mobile member of the party. She often ranges far and wide, scouting the countryside, determining what goods would be most profitable to buy or steal or smuggle on their travels. She also keeps an eye on regional politics and military movements, and she's not above making trouble if she spots some injustice going on. She acts as a bit of a messenger and scout for her Nameless Elder Mentor, and helps keep regional Lunars in loose touch. She has a bit of a crush on Strength-of-Many if she's met him. Rain is also lapsed priestess, so she keeps in touch with her spiritual side and has organized the ship's crew in worship of Luna and herself. She's been teaching her budding army of zealots her martial arts, and she makes it a habit to visit, drink tea and discuss spiritual matters with, and subsequently beat up martial artists up and down the coast to learn their styles.<br /> <br /> <b>Attrributes: </b>Str 4 Dex 5 Stam 3, Cha (F) 4 Man 2 App 3, Int 2 Per 4 Wit 3<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Martial Arts 3 (+1 Throwing People, +1 Unarmed, +1 Multiple Opponents), Archery 3, Resistance 2, Presence(F) 3 (+1 Intimidation), Survival(F) 1, Performance 2 (+1 Prayer), War 3 (+1 Desert Fighting), Medicine 1 (+1 Field Medic), Stealth 1, Awareness 3 (+1 From Above), Integrity 2 (+1 Never Give Up Hope), Occult 1, Lore 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Cult 2: Ship's Crew, Contacts 1: Monastic Martial Arts Community, Mentor 2: Some Old Lunar, Heart's Blood 2: (Mostly Birds, Snakes, Fish)<br /> <b>Charms+Knacks:</b><br /> -Hybrid Body Rearrangement<br /> -1st Dex Ex<br /> -Golden Tiger Stance<br /> -Flight of the Sparrow<br /> -Relentless Lunar Fury<br /> -1st Str Ex<br /> -Impressions of Strength (5BP)<br /> -1st Cha Ex<br /> -Cobra Hypnotic Method (5BP)<br /> -Face of the Moon Concealment (5BP)<br /> -Perception Excellency<br /> <b>BP Spent On:</b> 3 favored charms, Archery 3, MA Specialties<br /> <b>Notes on Building This Character: </b>So I had trouble here. I didn't want to take Deadly Beastman, because birds of prey are cool and all but deadly man-parrot just looks ridiculous. Weirdly? I'd be fine with a deadly dinosaur beastman with feathers, but...I dunno. Beaks just don't look that cool. Besides, I wanted a warrior defined by inhuman grace here. I went with Relentless Lunar Fury for that, going for a sort of zen battle-monk feel, where she just goes into the zone and starts killing people all River Tam style. Took Hybrid Body Rearrangement for a bag of neat tricks and for talon-hands if she needs them and for eagle-eyes when she's on the deck of the ship, took Golden Tiger Stance cuz cool name and because I like her not taking penalties as a mechanical representation of supernal grace. Flight of the Sparrow's for getting out of dodge if something too scary to handle shows up, and it's also for overland travel to support her messenger/scout role in the party. Impressions of Strength is a bag of neat tricks for one charm, and Cobra Hypnotic method makes her into a sacred battle-dancer instead of a smashy tank, which is more fun for me. I wanted lost more leading-combat-unit type charms, but she'll have to buy those with XP to grow into her role as a leader over time, just like she'll gradually pick up the entry-level moves of like a bunch of different Martial Arts styles. I Favored Presence instead of Martial arts for that reason: I'm not trying to be Optimal Build Guy here, just to build fun characters I'd wanna play. I wanted to give her some thaumaturgy to reflect her role as a battle priestess, but there was no space. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flyingspiderstudios.deviantart.com/art/Tu-Nung-424070072?ga_submit_new=10%253A1388675621\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Tu Nung (No Moon, Muskrat Totem)</b></a><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Concept: </b>Dirty Old Man, Wise Old Man, Cowardly Rogue, Cowardly Sorcerer, Shaman/Healer, Ship's Cook, Ship's Captain, Older Mentor-Figure. Tu Nung is a riverboat captain and the owner of the Gosling. He traded spices and herbs up and down the Meander, and also dealt in herbs and poisons. He loved traveling and seeing new places and learning new things, and he was a clever enough man that he made a decent and almost entirely illegal living, right up until he got caught and thrown in the hold of a Lookshyan naval vessel. He managed to escape by faking his own death using medicinal herbs he was conveniently smuggling at the time in...well, a place they didn't search. Luna took notice when he was drowning in a sack: he hadn't accounted for them throwing him in a bag with rocks and tossing him overboard so they didn't have to deal with the paperwork of a dead body. Within a week the odl bastard had conned his way into a small occult library, ownership of the Gosling, and a large pile of exotic herbs. He figured out enough sorcery out on the water to get in touch with the local elemental court, who got him in touch with an older Lunar who was passing through, and Tu Nung offered her a ride upriver in exchange for her tutelage: he knew all the tricks in the book, and he was gonna have to borrow some new books if the next couple centuries weren't gonna get boring. When playing Tu Nung, I want to remember the things that drew me to the Muskrat as his totem: the myth about the muskrat swimming to the bottom of the sea and bringing up the mud that became the world at the dawn of time, the muskrat's habit of building hidden underground bases with multiple exits, the muskrat's clearing wetlands of foliage which makes room for birds, the muskrat's stealing the food beavers store up for the winter, the building of woven-branch houses. He's a roguish trickster-figure, but he's also a character who plans ahead, someone who makes space for others and at the end of the day wants to create something meaningful and lasting, even if he doesn't know what yet.<br /> <br /> <b>Role In The Circle:</b> Tu Nung may not be the leader (that's sorta Rain's role), but he's the guy who brought everyone together. He found Nergui and Spring Rain with assistance from the local spirit courts, and he's the one who did both of their tattoos. He provides them with a home and mobile base of operations and a crew full of people to care about, to keep them grounded in their humanity. He also provides them with a wise (if roguish) father-figure who provides sage advice on life. He's a complete coward, and if a fight breaks out you can find him hiding below decks behind a dematerialized elemental bodyguard or two (the bodyguards give the player something to do so I'm not completely bored in combat). But his use of Monkey Shaping Emulation means he can forge any document the ship needs, and even make up fake valuables to sell at port, and The Spider's Trap Door comes in handy for smuggling pirated goods and hiding artifacts from Lookshyan and Realm port inspectors, and for hiding escaped slaves they're shipping to freedom. Tu Nung is the Resident Smart Guy, as the only one in the party with Intelligence over 2, and therefore he generally acts as the Master Planner who supports Spring's hopes and dreams or who figures out a way out of whatever mess Nergui has gotten into now. He's the party medic and the party chemist and the comic relief, and he makes a mean stew. He's also the shaman, and while Rain won't let him have any mind-enhancers aboard these days (she claims it's about getting rid of addictive substances as a means of Guild control, but he knows she's still not over her own addiction and is trying to avoid the temptation) he can still Vision-Quest and Spirit-Chat with the best of 'em. He keeps on good terms with the spirits, and is pretty good at arranging favorable weather with his summoned elemental allies. His studies of the tattoos have recently enabled him to figured out Harmony With Reality technique, and he's trying to get the party to sail out into Wyld Waters so he can make some fantasies real and sell them back in Creation where they'll make enough funds to build Spring that armada she's always wanted. If ever they run into a Big Nasty Spirit, Tu Nung plans on imprisoning it in his Tattoo Artifact Yasal Crystal (yeah, it's breaking the rules a little, but any shaman who can't imprison a demon in a tattoo isn't a REAL shaman, if you ask me).<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Str 2 Dex 3 Stam 2, Cha 3 Man(F) 4 App 2, Int 5 Per 3 Wit 4<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Occult (F): 3 (+1 Weather Spirits, +1 River Spirit Courts), Survival(F) 2, Lore 3 (+1 &quot;Have I Ever Told You About The Time I...&quot;), Medicine 3 (+1 Laughter Is The Best Medicine), Craft(Water) 3 (+1 Poisons), Sail 2, Performance 2 (+1 Bald-Faced Lies), Presence 2 , Stealth 3, Archery 3, Linguistics 1 (Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Spirit-Capturing Tat 3: (Tattoo Artifact. It's pretty much just a Yasal Crystal, but it can't let you use the spirit's charms-just trap the thing, bargain with it, and let it out), Resources 2: Ship+Smuggling Biz, Followers 2: Crew<br /> <b>Charms+Knacks:</b><br /> -Humble Mouse Technique<br /> -1st Int Ex<br /> -1st Percep Ex<br /> -1st Wits Ex<br /> -Monkey Shaping Emulation<br /> -Eye of the Cat<br /> -Form-Fixing Method<br /> -Harmony With Reality Technique<br /> -The Spider's Trap Door<br /> -Sorcery<br /> ---Summon Elemental<br /> <b>BP Spent on:</b> Essence 3: 7BP, Sorcery and a Spell<br /> <b>Notes on Building This Character: </b>Man, all the Lunar charms require Excellencies, and all the fun ones require higher Essence. Really looking forward to the ability to play Essence 1 in 3E. Having to take a slot for Sorcery that didn't net me any charms hurt, and so did not having room for thaumaturgy: by rights, this character really oughta know some rockin' alchemy rituals for potions and spells, he's very much a mix-a-potion sorta healer and poisoner. His anima doesn't do him much good, and he didn't have enough room to take the Master Manipulator charms he needs to turn into a true Master Planner. I also wanted to give him Dog Tongue Method so he could do the whole &quot;speak with animals&quot; thing and therefore be friends with Nergui's familiar, but maybe he'll learn that later. More spells'd be nice, though. That's probably where this budding sorcerer character'll end up spending his XP. Well, that and more space-warping Perception charms. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 01-02-2014, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:40:26-08:00","id":41161,"title":"","content":"If we understood what kind of point we were trying to prove (or disprove), I believe this experiment would provide much more useful information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:56:43-08:00","id":41167,"title":"","content":"I guess they're trying to get into fans heads or looking for patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:26:48-08:00","id":41188,"title":"","content":"Today I learned that I'm just the <i>worst</i> at building Lunars.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince-Among-Wolves, Full Moon Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Totem:</b> Blue Tiger<br /> <b>Strength 3</b>, <b>Dexterity 4</b>, <b>Stamina 3</b><br /> <b>Charisma 5</b>, Manipulation 2, Appearance 4<br /> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> Athletics 3, Awareness 2, Martial Arts 3, <b>Melee 5</b>, Presence 3, Resistance 3, Socialize 2, Stealth 3, <b>Survival 4</b><br /> <b>Specialties:</b> Melee: Hook Sword 3, Socialize: Courtly Intrigue 1<br /> <b>Languages:</b> Forest-tongue<br /> <br /> Compassion 4, Conviction 3, Temperance 1, Valour 4<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Artifact 1 (Behemothskin Coat), Artifact 1 (Hook Umbraklave), Influence 3, Resources 2<br /> <br /> <b>Knacks</b><br /> Beast-Power Concentration<br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> First Charisma Excellency<br /> Second Dexterity Excellency<br /> Claws of the Silver Moon<br /> Dog-Tongue Method<br /> Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance<br /> Golden Tiger Stance<br /> Perfect Fear Scent<br /> Terrifying Lust Infliction<br /> <br /> <b>Commentary:</b> The idea here was to have this sexy, regal death machine. Because building Solars and Abyssals have spoiled me (no Excellency prerequisites!), that ended up not happening. Still, she can defend her circlemates amicably well, seduce and intimidate, talk to animals, and gouge the fuck out of you with her off-hand using Claws of the Silver Moon.<br /> She has Beast-Power Concentration so that she can get the benefits of warform without pulling down a Wyld Hunt on the circle\u2019s heads.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Im Oman, Changing Moon Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Totem:</b> Centipede<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, <b>Stamina 4</b><br /> <b>Charisma 3</b>,<b> Manipulation 5</b>,<b> Appearance 3</b><br /> Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 4<br /> <br /> Awareness 2, Dodge 3, Integrity 3, Investigation 3, Larceny 2, Lore 1, <b>Presence 4</b>, Sail 3, Socialize 1, <b>Survival 2</b>, Thrown 2<br /> <b>Specialties:</b> Larceny: Legerdemain 1, Secret Societies 2, Presence: Blatant Lies 3<br /> <b>Languages:</b> Seatongue<br /> <br /> Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Temperance 4, Valour 2<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Hearthstone Bracers), Contacts 3, Heart\u2019s Blood 3, Manse 2<br /> <br /> <b>Knacks</b><br /> Changing Plumage Mastery<br /> Internal Form Mastery<br /> Humble Mouse Shape<br /> Prey\u2019s Skin Disguise<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> First Manipulation Excellency<br /> Butterfly Eyes Defense<br /> Chattering Magpie Inflection<br /> Hide of the Cunning Hunter<br /> Mirror Sight Dismay<br /> Shifting Penumbra Stance<br /> <br /> <b>Commentary:</b> A fast-talking trickster type, I guess. He has the seeming of a wise man, though, and his primary function in the group is to keep things together and not draw too much attention. He\u2019s also the most able shapeshifter, and the only one capable of taking human shapes, so infiltration tends to fall to him.<br /> In a hypothetical chronicle, he\u2019d eventually take all the Butterfly Eyes Charms, and the whole Scorpion and Toad tree \u2013 hence the Stamina.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>The Red Hands of Yowa, No Moon Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Totem:</b> Bearded Vulture<br /> Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> Charisma 3, <b>Manipulation 4</b>, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Perception 5</b>,<b> Intelligence 4</b>, <b>Wits 3</b><br /> <br /> Awareness 3, Dodge 2, Integrity 2, Linguistics 2, Lore 2, Medicine 3, Melee 1, <b>Occult 4</b>, Performance 3, Presence 1, <b>Survival 1</b>, War 2<br /> <b>Specialties:</b> Occult: the Dead 2, Occult: Sorcery 1, Performance: Prayer 1<br /> <b>Languages:</b> Old Realm, Seatongue, Skytongue<br /> <br /> Compassion 1, Conviction 2, Temperance 4, Valour 3<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Cult 3, Followers 3, Henchmen 2, Resources 1<br /> <br /> <b>Knacks</b><br /> Life of the Hummingbird<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> Second Intelligence Excellency<br /> Cold Breath of the Moon<br /> Flesh-Sculpting Art<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick<br /> <br /> <b>Spells</b><br /> Demon of the First Circle<br /> Empathic Wind<br /> <br /> <b>Thaumaturgy</b><br /> Banish the Faithless Servant<br /> Blood Magic<br /> Curse<br /> <br /> <b>Commentary: </b>The original conceit was this: \u201cWasp of the Labyrinth Trick is cool.\u201d Then I met the Essence prerequisite, and it was less cool.<br /> So the character ended up being a sorcerer instead, and a weird kind of behind-the-scenes support type. She won\u2019t be fighting much, but she can bolster her allies with intelligence, demons, zombies, and feather-cloaked ninjas. She can also do some healing with Flesh-Sculpting Art.<br /> Cold Breath of the Moon is just there because it\u2019s cool, and also because it doesn\u2019t require an Excellency. The thaumaturgy is likewise stylistic (blood sacrifice, yo).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:30:02-08:00","id":41190,"title":"","content":"I just switched to Windows 8 and I'm still trying to figure out how to juggle multiple PDFs, so I might forget something. Hopefully not.<br /> <br /> ========<br /> Full Moon:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Name: Southern Stampede<br /> Caste: Full Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Bull<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> <b>Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4</b><br /> Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Perception 4</b>, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <i>Combat is the only thing the Full Moon Caste is good for, so physical attributes are primary. Social charms have nothing important to contribute to combat, so they're tertiary. Mental attributes are more of a mixed big. Wits provides some stealth, but there's a lot of overlap with dexterity. Intelligence has the UMI defenses, so Intelligence 3 is mandatory. Perception charms start at Perception 3 and a lot of them require Perception 4, so that gets the loose Attribute dot Caste Lunars get.<br /> <br /> Used 9 bonus points to bring Strength from 3 to 5 and Dexterity from 4 to 5. </i><br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> <i>Martial Arts 5 (Claws of the Silver Moon +3)</i>,<br /> Integrity 3,<br /> Presence 2,<br /> Resistance 2,<br /> <i>Survival 2</i>,<br /> Lore 2,<br /> Athletics 2,<br /> Awareness 3,<br /> Dodge 3 (While Heavily Armoured +3),<br /> Linguistics 1,<br /> Socialize 2.<br /> <br /> <i>Ability-wise, I like well-rounded characters. Full Moons don't really need that many abilities, so they have a lot of dots to spare. I picked Martial Arts as the favoured ability so Martial Arts charms would be favoured and because Full Moons really benefit from unarmed combat. I took a Martial Arts speciality in Claws of the Silver Moon and a Dodge specialty for While Heavily Armoured because I couldn't think of anything else, mostly.<br /> <br /> Then I realized I had a spare bonus point and switched them around. +3 to Dodge While Heavily Armoured and +1 Martial Arts while using Claws of the Silver Moon. Used the Bonus Point to bring Claws of the Silver Moon up to +3.<br /> <br /> I used an additional 2 Bonus Points to get Martial Arts 5. </i><br /> <br /> Virtues<br /> Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Temperance 2, Valor 3<br /> <br /> <i>Nothing special here. Lunars only need one high virtue for their Essence pool, so Valor 3 and the others at 2 is fine. </i><br /> <br /> Backgrounds<br /> <br /> Backing 1 (Swords of Luna)<br /> Mentor 1<br /> Reputation 1<br /> Tattoo Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Hearthstone Bracers)<br /> Artifact 3 (Moonsilver Superheavy Plate)<br /> <br /> <i>Backing, Mentor and Reputation are standard for Lunars. This build doesn't require disguises, so the Tattoo Artifact isn't really a problem, plus it looks cool. It also means that I don't need to bother trying to hide the tell and moonsilver tattoos at all, so that's one more charm and one more knack to spare. I had two spare background dots, so I went for armour. Fuck Heart's Blood, it's just a waste of points and the only useful shapeshifting is DBT anyway.<br /> <br /> I used my last Bonus Point to upgrade my armour to Superheavy Plate. </i><br /> <br /> Knacks<br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation (Gazelle's Pace, Armored Hide)<br /> <br /> <i>Terrifying Beastman Alteration and Devastating Ogre Enhancement are probably the only other knacks I would ever get for this character. I could probably pick better mutations, but I don't really have time right now and I'm juggling three different PDFs as it is. </i><br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Excellencies: Dexterity (3rd), Perception (2nd)<br /> <br /> Strength: Claws of the Silver Moon, Impressions of Strength<br /> <br /> Stamina: Ox-Body Technique (x2)<br /> <br /> Dexterity: Golden Tiger Stance<br /> <br /> <i>I went for the 3rd Dex Excellency because my gut impression is that Lunars can add plenty of dice to their attacks without Excellencies and it's more mote-sustainable with Instinctive (Attribute) Unity. I've never actually run the numbers on that though, so I might be wrong. I picked the 2nd Perception Excellency just to get it out of the way and two Ox-Bodies because you can never go wrong with those. Claws of the Silver Moon buffs damage, Impressions of Strength adds some versatility and Golden Tiger Stance is a basic defense to supplement the massive soak. </i><br /> <br /> Essence 2 (Personal Motes 22, Peripheral Motes 40)<br /> <br /> Willpower 10<br /> <br /> <i>Base 5, plus 5 bonus points. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Very quickly eyeballing the numbers: 19 dice to attack, 8 dice of damage, 24L/24B Soak and DDV 6.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, while Full Moons are the easiest Lunars to make, I also find them the most boring. It's like all the decisions are pre-made. </i><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> ========<br /> Changing Moon:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Name: Shimmering Feather<br /> Caste: Changing Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Peacock<br /> <br /> <i>The Spirit Shape is completely irrelevant when making a Changing Moon, so I just went with something pretty. </i><br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Charisma 5, Manipulation 5, Appearance 5</b><br /> Perception 4, <b>Intelligence 4</b>, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <i>I wrote off combat entirely and decided to bet on Stamina for basic survivability. Social Attributes are primary for obvious reasons. Mental Attributes are more complicated. They all have charms that are useful to social combat, but none of them have </i>a lot<i> of charms that are useful to social combat. Wits seemed the least useful, so I dropped it a bit and brought Perception up to 4, because once again, there's no point in having Perception any lower. Added the extra dot to Intelligence and used 12 Bonus Points to max out the Social Attributes. </i><br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> Thrown 1,<br /> Integrity 3,<br /> <i>Performance 3 (Swaying the Crowd +2)</i>,<br /> Presence 3 (Negotiations +2),<br /> Resistance 2,<br /> <i>Survival 2</i>,<br /> Lore 2,<br /> Investigation 2,<br /> Occult 1,<br /> Bureaucracy 2,<br /> Linguistics 2,<br /> Socialize 2 (High Society +2).<br /> <br /> <i>Survival is only there because I'm forced to get it and Performance is only in there because it's exactly like Presence, only it deals with groups. The choice of a favoured ability is completely meaningless. I just picked Performance on a whim. I used 1 Bonus Point to get a specialty for Performance. </i><br /> <br /> Virtues<br /> Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Temperance 3, Valor 2<br /> <br /> <i>Same deal as above with the virtues. I just prioritized Temperance over Valor. Self-control seemed important for someone who probably hangs out at parties a lot. </i><br /> <br /> Willpower 10<br /> <br /> <i>Base 5, plus 5 from Bonus Points. </i><br /> <br /> Backgrounds<br /> Backing 1 (Winding Path)<br /> Mentor 1<br /> Reputation 1<br /> Resources 3<br /> Influence 1<br /> <br /> <i>Standard Lunar Background Package, plus something that looks appropriate to a rising local socialite. I'd add Contacts, but I had no more dots to spread around. </i><br /> <br /> Knacks<br /> Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> <br /> <i>Gotta do everything possible to hide the Tell. </i><br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Excellencies: Charisma (2nd)<br /> <br /> Stamina: Ox-Body Technique (x2)<br /> Charisma: Terrifying Lust Infliction<br /> Appearance: Hide of the Cunning Hunter<br /> Intelligence: Righteous Lion Defense, True-to-the-Pack Dedication<br /> <br /> <i>UMI defenses, plus a charm to hide the moonsilver tattoos. I wanted some Manipulation, but then I remembered I needed basic survivability and got Ox-Body Technique twice. Terrifying Lust Infliction seemed like the most useful charm for a socialite. Rouse up the party and all that. </i><br /> <br /> Essence (Personal Motes 22, Peripheral Motes 40)<br /> <br /> Willpower 10<br /> <br /> <i>Base 5, plus 5 from Bonus Points. </i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ========<br /> No Moon:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Name: Thousand Maws<br /> Caste: No Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Spider<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> Strength 2, <b>Dexterity 5</b>, Stamina 3<br /> Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Perception 4, Intelligence 4, Wits 4</b><br /> <br /> <i>Mental primary, Physical secondary and Social tertiary, which is fine because we're making a GIANT FUCKING SPIDER and nobody wants to talk to a GIANT FUCKING SPIDER anyway. Betting on Dex for combat. Spent the extra dot on Wits and 3 bonus points to bring Dex from 4 to 5. </i><br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> Archery 3 (Greater Natural Missile +3),<br /> Integrity 2,<br /> <i>Survival 2</i>,<br /> Investigation 2,<br /> Lore 2,<br /> <i>Occult 3</i>,<br /> Athletics 2,<br /> Awareness 2,<br /> Dodge 3,<br /> Stealth 3 (Ambushes +1),<br /> Linguistics 1.<br /> <br /> <i>Stealth build designed for long-range combat. </i><br /> <br /> Virtues<br /> Compassion 2, Conviction 3, Temperance 2, Valor 2<br /> <br /> <i>Same deal again with the virtues. </i><br /> <br /> Backgrounds<br /> Backing 1 (Crossroads Society)<br /> Mentor 1<br /> Reputation 1<br /> Tattoo Artifact 2 (Hearthstone Bracers)<br /> Manse 2 (Gemstone of Surface Thoughts)<br /> <br /> <i>I ran out of ideas after the Basic Lunar Background Package, so I just went with a safe bet. Disguise is not a priority, so tattoo artifacts aren't a problem. </i><br /> <br /> Knacks<br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation (Greater Natural Missile, Spinnerets), Perfected Hybrid Interaction<br /> <br /> <i>The Spinnerets could be replaced with Toxins. </i><br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Excellencies: Dexterity (3rd), Wits (1st)<br /> Strength: Claws of the Silver Moon<br /> Intelligence: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Wits: The Spider's Trap Door<br /> <br /> Spells: Death of Obsidian Butterflies<br /> <br /> <i>Claws of the Silver Moon can buff the Greater Natural Missile to buff its modest basic damage and The Spider's Trap Door handles stealth. It's a good combination for someone who fights through ambushes. I picked Death of Obsidian Butterflies to add some artillery power. </i><br /> <br /> Essence 3 (Personal Motes 23, Peripheral Motes 44)<br /> <br /> <i>Ten Bonus Points to get up to Essence 3 so we can have Sorcery. </i><br /> <br /> Willpower 10<br /> <br /> <i>Base 5, plus 5 from Bonus Points. </i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ========<br /> The Full Moon is a basic CQC monster. His job is to stand in the middle of the fight and take all the hits that the others can't take.<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon is there for social combat and can't do anything else. He's the most likely to further develop his shapeshifting in the future. I can't say he really complements the other Lunars - he has absolutely no synergy with them - but he's the only one who can deal with social situations that might come up.<br /> <br /> The No Moon is there to back up the Full Moon with ranged attacks. Perception and Wits have good synergy for a character that relies on ambushes, but they have very little synergy with Intelligence, so I added sorcery to make Intelligence more useful and increase the options for ranged attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 01-02-2014, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:54:38-08:00","id":41200,"title":"","content":"Tiger Mother of An-Teng - Warrior<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Motivation: Drive the Realm from An-Teng. She has Intimacies toward tigers (Adoration), the Pale Mistress (Appreciation), rebels against the Realm (Respect), the Scarlet Dynasty (Hatred) and those who willingly serve the Realm (Disdain).<br /> Caste: Full Moon<br /> Anima Banner: Rapidly flashing images of people and prey being torn to bloody giblets from the perspective of a tiger.<br /> Spirit Shape: Notably large tiger with well-kept coat<br /> Tell: Glow-reflective eyes<br /> Attributes: <i>Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4</i>; Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3; Perception 3, Intelligence 3, <i>Wits 4</i><br /> Virtues: Compassion 3, Conviction 2, Temperance 2, Valor 2<br /> Virtue Flaw: Curse of the Mother Hen<br /> Abilities: Athletics 3, Awareness 3, Craft (Wood) 2, Dodge 2 (Against Immaculate Martial Artists +1), Lore 1, <i>Martial Arts 5 (Tiger Style +3)</i>, Presence 2 (Scary +1), Resistance 3, Socialize 2 (Read Intent +2), Stealth 3 (Ambush +1), <i>Survival 5 (Raising Young Animals +3)</i>, War 1<br /> Backgrounds: Allies 3, Heart\u2019s Blood 2, Influence 1, Resources 1<br /> Knacks: Deadly Beastman Transformation (Acute Smell, Acute Hearing, Fur, Talons, Wolf\u2019s Pace)<br /> Charms:<br /> Excellencies: Dexterity (1<sup>st</sup>)<br /> Dexterity: Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance, Golden Tiger Stance<br /> Stamina: Hide-Toughening Essence<br /> Tiger Style: To Form, plus Celestial Tiger Hide<br /> Essence: 2<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> <br /> Rationale: Learning and relying on Tiger Style gives her room to grow into other, Lunar-specific routes of aggression. As a dedicated warrior, she cultivates methods other than the admittedly useful Claws of the Silver Moon, changing into beastman or spirit shape and calling upon her Style\u2019s Charms to shear through the enemy and cushion most of the damage. As a figure of guardianship, she can also easily swat aside challenges to her allies or charges, particularly if those with more blatant shortcomings.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> Maneater of Coral - Trickster<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Motivation: Take the heart and shape of every Sea Lord for the next millennium. The Maneater has Intimacies to Coral\u2019s Society (Hate), the other young women in the government counting house where she works (several Protective Friendships by individual), and the concept of the Tya (Resentment), the Realm (Sneering Joyous Criticism).<br /> Caste: Changing Moon<br /> Anima Banner: A serene splash of color that ripples like water, with an ominous shadow swimming underneath.<br /> Spirit Shape: An extremely well-fed pointer shark<br /> Tell: Rough skin<br /> Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3; <i>Charisma 3, Manipulation 5, Appearance 3</i>; Perception 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 3<br /> Virtues: Compassion 2, Conviction 4, Temperance 4, Valor 2<br /> Virtue Flaw: Curse of the Heartless Weasel<br /> Abilities: Archery 1, Athletics 2, Awareness 2, <i>Bureaucracy 5 (Accountancy +1)</i>, Lore 2, Martial Arts 3 (Chomp Chomp +1), Melee 1, Performance 2 (Political Grandstanding +1), Presence 2, Socialize 2 (No I Am Not A Lunar +1), Stealth 2, <i>Survival 2</i>, War 1<br /> Backgrounds: Allies 2, Contacts 3, Heart\u2019s Blood 3, Mentor 2, Resources 1<br /> Knacks: Prey\u2019s Skin Disguise, Towering Beast Form<br /> Charms:<br /> Excellencies: Manipulation (1<sup>st</sup>), Wits (1<sup>st</sup>)<br /> Strength: Claws of the Silver Moon<br /> Manipulation: Cat-Face Presentation, Mask of White Jade<br /> Appearance: Hide of the Cunning Hunter<br /> Essence: 2<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> <br /> Rationale: This character is meant to pull Havesh-style shenanigans, but she also has ambitions that go far beyond just being some spook that assassinates people. Her aim is to use the shapes that she collects as a stepping stone to becoming like His Divine Lunar Presence from Heaven\u2019s Reach. Claws of the Silver Moon is an excellenct one-stop shop to be threatening in combat, which suits her assassination methods well enough and can provide some defensive measures if she is without a weapon as well. Her social Charms help to keep her true nature concealed from prying eyes and at the same time allow her to maneuver in political arenas while using the faces of her victims. Finally, she\u2019ll need to invest in Wits in the future to conceal her magical nature more effectively, so she has an Excellency there.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Swamp Bastard - Shaman<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Motivation: Terrorize Greyfalls into utter uselessness to the Realm. The Swamp Bastard has Intimacies toward his Manse (Jealously Possessive), his armor (Jealously Possessive), the village closest to his Manse (Valued Conveniences) and the Realm (Fuck The Police)<br /> Caste: No Moon<br /> Anima Banner: Background of dark mud on which gator tracks spontaneously appear, as if an invisible animal were walking across it.<br /> Spirit Shape: Huge, silvery-blue gator<br /> Tell: Smell of the swamp<br /> Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, <i>Stamina 4</i>; Charisma 1, Manipulation 4, Appearance 2; Perception 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 4<br /> Virtues: Compassion 1, Conviction 3, Temperance 3, Valor 2<br /> Virtue Flaw: Curse of the Humble Sloth<br /> Abilities: Athletics 1, Awareness 2, Dodge 2, Investigation 1, Lore 2, Martial Arts 2, Medicine 3 (Psychological Health +1), Occult 5, Presence 1, Resistance 1, Stealth 3 (In Swamp +2), Survival 5 (Swamp +1), Thrown 1<br /> Backgrounds: Artifact 3 (Moonsilver Superheavy Plate), Manse 4 (produces a Stone of Dream Entrance), Resources 1<br /> Knacks: Towering Beast Form<br /> Charms:<br /> Excellencies: Intelligence (1<sup>st</sup>)<br /> Strength: Subduing the Honored Foe<br /> Stamina: Armor-Forming Technique<br /> Intelligence: Mandate of the Hungry Mouse, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Wits: Thousandfold Wasp Dance<br /> Spells: Dragon of Smoke and Flame<br /> Essence: 3<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> <br /> Rationale: He found his Manse via his spell, and terrorizes the Realm\u2019s holdings with Mandate of the Hungry Mouse. He has enough resilience to weather some terrible assaults, and his capacity to spit out a cloud of stinging, swarming insects aids in both the mysterious, strange shaman image and, like Subduing the Honored Foe, knock out enemies, who will then be the victims of dream invasion via his Hearthstone. His Intelligence Excellency helps to put some more power behind Mandate of the Hungry Mouse, as well as to provide the opened gateway to Flesh-Sculpting Art, which can both be used to heal and to make those whom he has knocked out look like someone else, of potential utility if a trickster-type comrade needs or simply wishes for a doppelganger target to stay alive, such as if running a decoy shell game during a military operation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T11:41:25-08:00","id":41217,"title":"","content":"Okay, I have enough test samples now. Thanks, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T11:45:02-08:00","id":41220,"title":"","content":"So what were you looking for anyway? Making sure the concepts still are possible in 3E or getting a feel for what the community expect to do with a lunar PC or what? I'd love to hear what you're thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:10:44-08:00","id":41232,"title":"","content":"Drat! I was preparing my writeups, but being at work is kinda prohibitive.<br /> <br /> I'll at least post the concepts (these were an actual Lunar circle in a game once, was trying to re-create their writeups for I haven't their charsheets).<br /> <br /> Gran Fortress: Full Moon Strength-based lunar with a sea-turtle totem. Proficient in hand-to-hand (tattoo smashfists and god-kicking boots) and Archery (twin Essence Cannons). Also owned a moon-faced spiked tower shield that would become/meld into his carapace in war form.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Scale: crocodile-totemed, charisma-based Changing Moon. Uses communication, training and territory charms (as well as his manse) to create guerrilla units of how-are-all-these-animals-so-well-coordinated (also beastmen)?! Also a fan of hypnosis (cobra-hypnotic/forgetful victim), impersonation and cannibalism.<br /> <br /> Auspicious Jellyfish (can't remember actual name):<br /> Jellyfish-totemed No-Moon artificer-sorceror. Maintained Gran's Essence Cannons but had a love for poisons and acids, especaly crafted and/or sorcerous ones (demonic included). (Scorpion-toad charm tree is a favorite of his). Favorite pass-times include transforming into a jellyfish and flopping around on the floor proclaiming &quot;I'm a jellyfish *repeat cheek-flopping noise*&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-02-2014, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:13:00-08:00","id":41234,"title":"","content":"Dammit I just finished my third :P, oh well, care to divulge the purpose of these characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:57:27-08:00","id":41262,"title":"","content":"Dang! I just finished the Bikini Bottom Trio... But nevermind, it was a real pain in the ass going through MoEP, GotMH, Ink Monkeys and Scroll of Errata... FUCK YOU Ex2!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T13:50:32-08:00","id":41300,"title":"","content":"Oh, already over? Thank you very much for letting us know; I'd just been planning things out. While looking things over made me more enthusiastic about the Full Moon and Changing Moon than expected, the No Moon teacher/martial artist left me just as disappointed as last time. Was not looking forward to that. For some of my grievances/complaints as I went through, see the spoiler below.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wolf Pack Training Technique is strictly martial-related teaching, which -- outside Martial Arts -- isn't at all what the concept is after. Still, it's the only canon people-teaching Charm so hey. For its prerequisites, there's Dog Tongue Method (I'm perfectly fine with this), Nature-Reinforcing Allocation (doesn't fit the concept I wanted at all), Sharing the Gifts of Luna (a cool thing I would totally snag down the road, but wanted more personal prowess before picking up), and a Charisma Excellency (handy, but really doesn't feel necessary). That's a lot of Charms to get at the only teaching Charm. After a survivability purchase or two, there's no real room for MA or much else to start.<br /> <br /> Sorcery doesn't suit the concept, which is good and bad. If it did, there'd be no real Charm decisions at all. On the other hand, the No Moon anima is mostly dead weight (a -1 external penalty to attackers is something, at least).<br /> <br /> Was also not looking forward to deciding on a Favored Attribute that might not be Dexterity (already kinda invested in Charisma...). Ditto deciding on a Favored Ability that might not be Martial Arts (Lore/Occult on a teacher just makes sense). Glah...</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-02-2014, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T13:57:31-08:00","id":41302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41161#post41161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we understood what kind of point we were trying to prove (or disprove), I believe this experiment would provide much more useful information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unbiased answers might be more valuable than answers that are geared towards trying to prove a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/41-silverwinglie","name":"silverwinglie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar41_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T14:16:18-08:00","id":41315,"title":"","content":"Afterthought: I'm, again, somewhat-ashamed of the fruit of my efforts; I'm almost certain that I could have gotten the sort of effects I wanted with raksha Grace artifacts, but it kinda feels like cheating; after all, I'm assuming John M\u00f8rke wanted these for their actual capabilities, and not just what Artifacts I could abuse using Fair Folk rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T14:28:33-08:00","id":41325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41300#post41300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, already over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but fuck it, I'm going to do it anyway because I want to. I just won't be doing it right exactly now because I got shit coming up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T16:41:38-08:00","id":41393,"title":"","content":"I came up with a circle that I liked and am going to expand upon later. Keep in mind that I haven't read anything Lunar in a while. I'm sure there will be things 'wrong' with these characters (constructive criticism only please). Also, I'm still working on the characterization of barbarians/savages. If these ever make it to full-fledged characters expect much more than what I have down here, I hope to make mine as interesting as any other society in Exalted.<ul><li>Howl Triumphant (physical, wits): Ram-totem Full Moon. Born in Great Forks to a minor noble house, she exalted while on a hunting trip with his Immaculate private high school. Her former peers turned on her, calling her an Anathema. Four years later she now eschews the pampered trappings of his youth, instead she studies to be a warlord under her mentor the Clawed Czar: a powerful Lunar based in the Northeast. Her previously calm demeanor has turned brash and a bit feral, although she still remembers a surprising amount from her noble upbringing. Howl has focused her training on war and leadership: war to bring the surrounding tribes under her Czar's rule and leadership to turn these swords outwards to strike at the rest of the world. She uses her charms to intimidate, to subjugate, and to kill. She is the only one of the group to have mastered the Deadly Beastman Transformation, and is debatably the most deadly of the Circle.</li> <li>Kit Dayan (social, dexterity): Fox-totem Changing Moon. Kit is a charming young Haslanti, newly arrived in the Northeast. His fortunes were changed drastically by his exaltation \u2013 the formerly worthless son of a poor airshipman was now one of the most powerful people in the North. After a short time 'consulting' with the Haslanti government, made more difficult by his casteless nature, he found an elder to tattoo him. This elder gave him a mission: to infiltrate the war council of the Bull of the North. Unfortunately Kit overestimated his abilities, tried to seduce the Bull, and had to flee the North. Now he is a wanderer, having recently arrived in the Northeast he has cast his fate with his circle in order to accomplish daring deeds. Kit is devilishly clever and somewhat selfish. However, he's everything but stupid and does value and rely on the worth of his companions. He uses his charms to deceive, to hunt, and to seduce. Kit has drank the most heart's blood and has the largest library of animal shapes.</li> <li>Whispering Mask (mental, manipulation): Owl-totem No Moon. Mask has known no life but that of the savage. Born into the rule of the Clawed Czar, she knows the code of honor that binds the Northern barbarians better than either of her comrades. Trained as a shaman, she exalted while imprisoned after a tribal raid. In her fury escaping, she ripped apart the rival tribe into pieces with her claws, with her tongue, and with her mind. Her display of might, both physical and sorcerous, has caused them to deify her and they now serve as her cult. Returning to her home, her argent anima banner whipping around her, she has assumed the mantle of shaman and is now working towards unlocking the power of First Circle Sorcery. Mask is strong-willed and forceful. Her only goal is to grow in power and to bring the rest of the world under the heel of the Clawed Czar. She uses her charms to perceive, to protect, and to ensorcel. Mask already has knowledge of sorcerous workings and is close to learning First Circle Sorcery.</li> </ul>EDIT: If anyone wants to pick out charms for these three please feel free","signature":"","edited":{"userid":259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","user":"Overshee","date":". 01-02-2014, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T17:47:08-08:00","id":41422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41217#post41217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have enough test samples now. Thanks, everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what were you trying to test, out of curiosity? Whether or not they could be made using 3e Lunar chargen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T18:19:21-08:00","id":41431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41422#post41422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what were you trying to test, out of curiosity? Whether or not they could be made using 3e Lunar chargen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just from looking at the big \u00d8's avatar, it's clear that he's a mad scientist of some sort. Who knows what manner of maniacal experiments he's performing on the Lunar Exalted in his laboratory of words?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T18:58:45-08:00","id":41450,"title":"","content":"Aww. I was gonna see if I could sit down this weekend and build a Lunar Leverage Crew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T20:36:48-08:00","id":41483,"title":"","content":"Alchemicals would be better just because they have more castes, but still, that is a tremendous idea, BrilliantRain. What would Elliot's totem be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:33:08-08:00","id":41509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41483#post41483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals would be better just because they have more castes, but still, that is a tremendous idea, BrilliantRain. What would Elliot's totem be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not specifically the crew from Leverage, just a group in that style.<br /> <br /> More specifically, here was my idea: John specifically said &quot;Make three 2.5 Lunar characters, one of each caste, with starting character creation rules. Make each caste compliment the other, with mostly different Charms. Make each caste perform to the typical role of its caste.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, to me, Lunars are generally the 'less obvious' types. Stealthy instead of loud, sneaky instead of straightforward, and so on. In contrast to the Solars who use magic that usually relies on overwhelming power and direct force. So, a trio of Lunar noble thieves seems like it would work for the theme. Plus, since I can follow the Heist conventions, it should be easier to find ways for the trio to compliment each other, again, as requested.<br /> <br /> The Full Moon would be focused on Intrusion and Combat. Athletics, Larceny, Stealth, anything needed to get in somewhere they're not supposed to be. Also enough combat capability to defeat five normal people and at least hold off a supernatural opponent long enough for the others to escape. (Parker and Elliot)<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon would be their Grifter, someone capable of taking on any form, an expert in social fu, and a master of convincing people to do things without them realizing it. (Sophie)<br /> <br /> The No Moon would be the Mastermind, Sorcerer, and Magical Security Expert. They'd be the one casing the joint, making the plans, and figuring out where the thing is kept, what the mark's flaws are, backing up the grifter's aliases, and so on. (Nate and Hardison).<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, for the record, it's been a long time since I cracked the cover of 2e Lunars. I remember some of the charms and knacks and things, but I don't remember the details or the trees, nor do I know how they changed in 2.5. So I have no idea how doable those descriptions are. Still, I'd think it would be reasonable to get something that approached the above characters. I'll try to post the sheets on Sunday or Monday, so that you can have an 'After' picture to go with this 'Before.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T22:11:48-08:00","id":41518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41431#post41431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just from looking at the big \u00d8's avatar, it's clear that he's a mad scientist of some sort. Who knows what manner of maniacal experiments he's performing on the Lunar Exalted in his laboratory of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>... Something different from the Lunar experiments in your lab?<br /> <br /> We <a href=\"http://titotravels.files.wordpress.com/2013/04/screen-shot-2013-03-19-at-6-26-55-pm.png\" target=\"_blank\">sent </a>in <a href=\"http://bntp-production.imgix.net/uploads/posts/image/15339/guinea-pig.jpg?crop=top&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=500\" target=\"_blank\">spies </a><a href=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/_-3a_PULLdkA/THy8rKyheFI/AAAAAAAAA_g/be3QjJaz62g/s400/dogarmor.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">you </a><a href=\"http://media-cache-ec0.pinimg.com/236x/3d/a9/c2/3da9c24c0509ee3f345aac0637033b3a.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">see</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T23:11:35-08:00","id":41542,"title":"","content":"...I only did write ups for two and I haven't posted them yet.<br /> <br /> Heck with it, I'll post them tomorrow so they don't go to waste. Just need to do the Full Moon. Maybe I should give him Essence 3...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:02:09-08:00","id":41688,"title":"","content":"Oh well I guess it was good I checked the thread before I started working on these... fun with phone company mixed with prep for my Sidereal game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T13:01:29-08:00","id":41897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41431#post41431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just from looking at the big \u00d8's avatar, it's clear that he's a mad scientist of some sort. Who knows what manner of maniacal experiments he's performing on the Lunar Exalted in his laboratory of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dr. M\u00f8rkeable needs a Sing-Along Blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T23:50:29-08:00","id":42735,"title":"","content":"Can I just say that I really enjoyed reading the inline rationales for a lot of these? It was kinda nice knowing everyone else seems to have the same &quot;oh crap I needed that didn't I? Dammit what am I going to gimp just so I can have something resembling functionality?&quot; reactions to character gen that I always seem to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/698-chalicier","name":"chalicier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T00:07:09-08:00","id":42739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=41431#post41431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just from looking at the big \u00d8's avatar, it's clear that he's a mad scientist of some sort. Who knows what manner of maniacal experiments he's performing on the Lunar Exalted in his laboratory of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I cannot possibly think of a better time to use this, ever.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://www.kuroneko-chan.com/echoes/images/showtime.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i463.photobucket.com/albums/qq354/saisoua/Funny/Big-o.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:04:58-08:00","id":42884,"title":"","content":"Is it possible that the traditional three Lunar Castes simply aren't as helpful as those of other splats?<br /> <br /> Every other Caste or Aspect in the game is capable of handling the physical, social and mental tasks of their archetypes, roles, or functions.<br /> <br /> A Full Moon is capable of handling physical tasks which may have <i>nothing </i>to do with his or her character concept, in exchange for the inability to favor <i>both </i>the relevant social and mental Attribute for that concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:16:08-08:00","id":42889,"title":"","content":"Castes are there to provide roles for characters, structure for the splats and synergy between their Abilities/Attributes and it is necessary for something to fulfill those functions. Without Castes, you would need to present the same information without any structure to frame it. The splats would become incoherent.<br /> <br /> My impression is that the Alchemical Castes perform those functions admirably, but that Lunar Castes were designed to provide structure and synergy first and then had the roles tact on afterwards. Their roles are Physical, Social and Mental, but those aren't actually roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:25:09-08:00","id":42891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42889#post42889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that ...Lunar Castes were designed to provide structure and synergy first and then had the roles tact on afterwards. Their roles are Physical, Social and Mental, but those aren't actually roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm asking if anyone else suspects that this is a real problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:43:12-08:00","id":42899,"title":"","content":"I wonder if that means Lunars should have Aspects instead of Castes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:54:58-08:00","id":42908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42899#post42899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if that means Lunars should have Aspects instead of Castes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe like Devil Tigers have a Mythos from which their Charms and unique Caste derives, Lunars might simply have individual, unique Totems, with Totemic Attributes rather than Caste Attributes.<br /> <br /> Other splats don't have Totems. Maybe a splat which has Totems doesn't benefit from also having Castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-05-2014, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:57:33-08:00","id":42909,"title":"","content":"I grow annoyed at the incompatibility of this forum with iPhones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:14:52-08:00","id":42922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42891#post42891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm asking if anyone else suspects that this is a real problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only for the baggage associated with the word warrior. It doesn't quite get along with the decidedly inhuman ways of how Lunars engage in a fight. Shamans are associated with a close ties to the spirit, tricksters conjure up images of Coyote and Loki, but warrior is more of an incidental occupation which often demands attention from outside the Full Moon's schedule of exemplary qualities (i.e. Physical Attributes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:46:04-08:00","id":42946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42899#post42899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if that means Lunars should have Aspects instead of Castes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see this discussed in its own thread. It sounds extremely promising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:09:22-08:00","id":42955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=42946#post42946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to see this discussed in its own thread. It sounds extremely promising.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/42951-lunars-castes-or-aspects\">Done.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T02:16:20-08:00","id":43400,"title":"","content":"I saw this thread a few hours after it was originally posted and I thought to myself that this would be fun. I grabbed the <b>Manual of Exalted Power - Lunars</b> and <b>Glories to the Most High</b> and started reading through the Charms.<br /> <br /> Much to my surprise I was unable to come up with anything good. At all.<br /> <br /> I then realized that these were the first non-NPC Lunars I had ever attempted to make. When I make NPC Lunars I usually start with their function in regards to the plot and then I choose a cool Totem. And usually I just give them whatever Charms, Attributes, and Knacks they need to exemplify their Totems and fulfill their roles in the plot.<br /> <br /> I can usually make an interesting starting player character of any splat (I have never made a non-NPC Infernal, though, so they may be in the same bag as Lunars), but I keep drawing a blank on Lunars. There are interesting Charms in regards to Intelligence (though there are definitely too few of these) and breeding, but they are not exactly starting character material.<br /> <br /> Meh.<br /> <br /> I support replacing Castes with Totems because Totem pretty much always comes before Caste anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T02:28:00-08:00","id":43403,"title":"","content":"I can make Lunars just fine, they're just fucking awful as starting characters because there's a lot of charms/knacks I look at and go &quot;hmm that could be the basis of a character concept... <b>if it wasn't minimum essence 4+</b>&quot; the spine of my MoEP: Lunars is broken from a time when I threw it in frustration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T04:43:04-08:00","id":43439,"title":"","content":"This exercise has taught me the mechanics for Lunars bear out the narrative of their place on the bottom of the totem pole in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:03:17-08:00","id":43464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=43403#post43403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can make Lunars just fine, they're just fucking awful as starting characters because there's a lot of charms/knacks I look at and go &quot;hmm that could be the basis of a character concept... <b>if it wasn't minimum essence 4+</b>&quot; the spine of my MoEP: Lunars is broken from a time when I threw it in frustration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the great poison to be Excellency prerequisites, which require you to waste your fairly limited starting Charms and bonus points to get anything even resembling breadth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:15:11-08:00","id":43466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=43464#post43464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the great poison to be Excellency prerequisites, which require you to waste your fairly limited starting Charms and bonus points to get anything even resembling breadth.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh the ultimate two broken knees of lunars, requirements that are way that are two high and to many charms require excellency to get to anything useful. saddening to be honest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:12:20-08:00","id":43489,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Those two were problematic wherever they came up in 2nd edition. They just come up so often with Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:37:07-08:00","id":43503,"title":"","content":"Just drop the pre-reqs on all their Knacks and Charms by 1 Attribute and 1 Essence. Nothing breaks, I promise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:52:45-08:00","id":43516,"title":"","content":"Eh, you still have the ever-present Excellency prerequisites. Combined with the extremely limited number of Charms, you still feel like a nerfed version of your character concept. Or at least I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:56:51-08:00","id":43518,"title":"","content":"As long as Minimums are being blanket-adjusted -- with which I certainly agree with Dayen, for anyone trying to use 2e Lunars -- ignoring all/most of the Excellency pre-reqs is probably a good practice, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:00:50-08:00","id":43523,"title":"","content":"Along with stripping out prerequisite Excellencies, you'd also need to institute an overall consolidation of Charms to reduce the number of them significantly. They're supposed to be broader for Lunars, yet so many of them seem Solar-narrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=43503#post43503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just drop the pre-reqs on all their Knacks and Charms by 1 Attribute and 1 Essence. Nothing breaks, I promise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most will probably need the minimum Attribute knocked down by 2. Even given the assumption of 9/7/5 for Attributes, four dots of Strength is way too high for Impressions of Strength, and four dots of Perception is too high for... really, that's the vast, uncomfortable majority of Perception Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:24:40-08:00","id":43783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=43518#post43518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as Minimums are being blanket-adjusted -- with which I certainly agree with Dayen, for anyone trying to use 2e Lunars -- ignoring all/most of the Excellency pre-reqs is probably a good practice, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a trade-off with this decision that I'm not 100% comfortable with. A lot of the 'first' Charms in the Lunar charmset are designed to be gated. As speedbump Charms go, excellencies are hardly bad ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=43523#post43523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Along with stripping out prerequisite Excellencies, you'd also need to institute an overall consolidation of Charms to reduce the number of them significantly. They're supposed to be broader for Lunars, yet so many of them seem Solar-narrow.<br /> <br /> Most will probably need the minimum Attribute knocked down by 2. Even given the assumption of 9/7/5 for Attributes, four dots of Strength is way too high for Impressions of Strength, and four dots of Perception is too high for... really, that's the vast, uncomfortable majority of Perception Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can drop everything by 1 across the board and absolutely nothing bad happens. You need to be a lot more careful with two dot drops, which really requires know your way around the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I agree it's not ideal, but it's a solid step forward. Consolidating Charms is definitely a good idea, but also simply taking ones that are currently stand-alone Reflexive 1/2s and Supplementals and turning them into permanent upgrades to the &quot;base&quot; Charm in that particular tree also works fairly well. Some need some real love to be worth 10xp, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:47:09-08:00","id":43795,"title":"","content":"Well, almost every game of Exalted I wrote up characters for ever gave out free Excellencies anyway, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:36:50-08:00","id":43820,"title":"","content":"EX3 will give characters a free Excellency in each Ability/Attribute they have as Caste/Favored. This will free up Charm purchases at character creation as well as make it easier to purchase Charms with Excellency prereqs. So that's one problem solved, IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:56:12-08:00","id":43836,"title":"","content":"I'm not as familiar with Lunar Charms as I am with other charmsets, but I tried to make the concepts complimentary - not sure how much I succeeded, since I'm not up on the math, but these are the three I designed:<br /> <br /> Full Moon: Wolf Warrior, swift-acting bodyguard; Favored: Perception, Melee<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4, Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Perception 4, Charisma 3, Appearance 2, Manipulation 2<br /> Abilities: Survival 3, Melee 3, War 2, Martial Arts 3, Resistance 3, Integrity 3, Dodge 2, Athletics 3, Awareness 2, Thrown 1<br /> Backgrounds: Artifact 2 (Pair of Moonsilver Short Daiklave), Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Lamellar), Heart\u2019s Blood 1, Cult 2<br /> Knacks: Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> Charms: First Strength Exaltation, Wind-Wings Carry Technique, Relentless Lunar Fury, Ox-Body Technique, Hide Toughening Essence, Wasp-Sting Blur, Twin-Fang Technique, Frenzied Boar Fortification (5 BP)<br /> Essence 3<br /> Virtues: Valor 4, Compassion 1, Conviction 2, Temperance 2<br /> <br /> Changing Moon: Spymaster; Favored: Perception, Martial Arts<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Perception 4, Charisma 4, Manipulation 5, Appearance 3<br /> Abilities: Survival 2, Martial Arts 2, Melee 1, Integrity 3, Resistance 1, Dodge 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 1, Stealth 3, Presence 2, Investigation 2, Larceny 2<br /> Knacks: Prey\u2019s Skin Disguise<br /> Charms: Third Manipulation Excellency, False Burrow Pursuit, Butterfly Eyes Defense, Chattering Magpie Inflection, First Dexterity Excellency, Ground-Denying Defense, Ox-Body Technique, Counting the Elephant\u2019s Wrinkles, First Charisma Excellency<br /> Backgrounds: Heart\u2019s Blood 3, Resources 3, Contacts 3, Artifact 2 (Mask), Cult 2, Artifact 2 (Razor Claws), Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Buff Jacket)<br /> Virtues: Valor 2, Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Temperance 3<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> New Moon: Sorcerer; Favored: Dexterity; Occult<br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Perception 3, Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 1<br /> Abilities: Survival 2, Melee 3, Integrity 3, Resistance 3, Dodge 2, Occult 3, Lore 3, Medicine 2, Awareness 1, War 3<br /> Charms: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery, Spider\u2019s Trap Door, First Wits Excellency, Burgeoning Wyld Infliction, Second Intelligence Excellency, First Perception Excellency, Wyld-Sensing Instincts<br /> Knack: Hybrid Body Rearrangement<br /> Backgrounds: Cult 3, Artifact 1 (Short Daiklave), Artifact 2 (Moonsilver Buff Jacket), Manse 3, Heart\u2019s Blood 2, Followers 1<br /> Essence 3<br /> Virtues: Valor 1, Compassion 1, Conviction 4, Temperance 3<br /> <br /> The concept is that the trio are living out in the Northern or Eastern portion of the world, near the Bordermarches (possibly within). The New Moon Sorcerer is the brains of the operation, and typically stays at the groups hideout (his Manse). He uses BWI to give temporary mutations as needed to his allies, in case they need anything special for a mission, and to his followers to enhance their abilities to defend him, but his cowardice keeps him from the field unless absolutely necessary.<br /> Typically, it isn't necessary - his Changing Moon uses her Mask artifact to mimic him when necessary to interact with the rest of the world (the New Moon typically interacts with his Cult). When she's able to operate alone, she uses her techniques to become the perfect spy, infiltrating enemy encampments and local settlements.<br /> The Full Moon is a bodyguard, either as visible muscle for the Changing when she is out in public, a public distraction when she's working on infiltration, or a protector for the New Moon otherwise. He's not very subtle, and isn't supposed to be, but he also isn't an idiot by any means, and is in fact a very tactically minded individual. His charms focus on allowing him to act fast and take blows when necessary, then deal the damage back.<br /> I'm not sure if they work to enhance each other, but there's the concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T05:02:00-08:00","id":44081,"title":"","content":"I gave it a new try and I came up with a character I would actually love to play.<br /> <br /> <u>Caste:</u><br /> Full Moon<br /> <br /> <u>Spirit Shape:</u><br /> Howler Monkey<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue Flaw:</u><br /> The Curse of the Raging Bull<br /> <br /> <u>Motivation:</u><br /> Keep Creation from ever falling silent<br /> <br /> <u>Notable Intimacies:</u><br /> Adorjan (Hate), Silence (Unease), Swords of Luna (Loyalty)<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes:</u><br /> <b>Strength </b>3<br /> <b>Dexterity </b>4<br /> <b>Stamina </b>4<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma </b>4<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 3<br /> <br /> Perception 2<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities:</u><br /> Athletics 2<br /> Awareness 1<br /> Integrity 3<br /> Lore 2<br /> Martial Arts 3<br /> Occult 2<br /> <b>Performance</b> 3<br /> Presence 3<br /> Resistance 1<br /> <b>Survival</b> 2<br /> War 3<br /> <br /> <u>Knacks:</u><br /> Green Sun Child<br /> <br /> <u>Stamina Charms:</u><br /> Fish or Fowl Gestation<br /> Tiger and Seahorse Dynasty<br /> <br /> <u>Charisma Charms:</u><br /> First Charisma Excellency<br /> Foe-Turning Rebuke<br /> Maintaining the Pack<br /> Outworld-Forsaking Stance<br /> <br /> <u>Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style Charms:</u><br /> Inspiring Battle Hymn<br /> Terrifying Battle Shriek<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds:</u><br /> Cult 1<br /> Followers 2<br /> Influence 1<br /> Reputation 2<br /> Tattoo Artifact 1 (Breastplate)<br /> <br /> Essence: 3<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> <br /> <u>Virtues:</u><br /> Compassion 2<br /> Conviction 2<br /> Temperance 2<br /> Valor 3<br /> <br /> <u>Thoughts on the process:</u><br /> I wanted to make a Full Moon who was a warrior and a part of the Swords of Luna, protecting Creation against its outworld enemies, but I wanted to steer away from the hulking Deadly Beastman type of character, fighting Fair Folk at the edge of Creation. I am fascinated by howler monkeys, and I liked the idea of combining this totem with Charms from the Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. He is not a great warrior (again, compared to the hulking Deadly Beastman type) as his voice is greatest weapon, but in addition to the Martial Arts Charms I have chosen some Charisma Charms that should at least help him when fighting creatures of Darkness such as, for example, demons. I picture him leading a tribe of howler monkey beastmen, and I wanted him to have both some Breeding Charms and some Military Unit Charms to reinforce this. If his voice is his primary weapon, his followers are his secondary weapon. Once he reaches Essence 5, I am going for the Demon-Wracking Shout from <b>Manual of Exalted Powers - Infernals</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 01-07-2014, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:02:50-08:00","id":44342,"title":"","content":"<u><img src=\"http://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2012/10/29/article-2224727-15BDEAFF000005DC-687_634x447.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Caste:</u><br /> No Moon<br /> <br /> <u>Spirit Shape:</u><br /> Pink Underwing Moth Caterpillar<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue Flaw:</u><br /> The Curse of the Heartless Veasel<br /> <br /> <u>Motivation:</u><br /> Protect people from false religions<br /> <br /> <u>Notable Intimacies:</u><br /> The Immaculate Order (Contempt)<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes:</u><br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 2<br /> Stamina 4<br /> <br /> Charisma 4<br /> <b>Manipulation</b> 5<br /> Appearance 2<br /> <br /> <b>Perception </b>3<br /> <b>Intelligence </b>3<br /> <b>Wits</b> 3<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities:</u><br /> Athletics 1<br /> Awareness 2<br /> Integrity 3<br /> Linguistics 2<br /> Lore 3<br /> Martial Arts 2<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 3<br /> <b>Presence</b> 3<br /> Resistance 1<br /> Stealth2<br /> <b>Survival</b> 2<br /> <br /> <u>Knacks:</u><br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> Emerald Grasshopper Form<br /> Humble Mouse Shape<br /> <br /> <u>Charisma Charms:</u><br /> Perfect Fear Scent<br /> Second Charimas Excellency<br /> <br /> <u>Intelligence Charms:</u><br /> Counting the Elephant's Wrinkles<br /> <br /> <u>Manipulation:</u><br /> False Burrow Pursuit<br /> First Manipulation Excellency<br /> Mirror Sight Dismay<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds:</u><br /> Allies 3<br /> Cult 2<br /> Reputation 1<br /> Solar Bond 1<br /> <br /> Essence: 3<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> <br /> <u>Virtues:</u><br /> Compassion 1<br /> Conviction 3<br /> Temperance 3<br /> Valor 2<br /> <br /> <u>Thoughts on the process:</u><br /> I wanted to make a Full Moon shaman and iconoclast opposing the Immaculate Order, but more than anything I wanted the visuals of the Pink Underwing Moth Caterpillar (because that thing looks awesome and will look even more awesome in Deadly Beastman Shape). I wanted the character to be super smart, scary, and tricky and I chose Charms based around this. With the visuals of the totem and the Manipulation Charms I want the character to be a nightmarish creature straight out of a Hayao Miyazaki movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:15:49-08:00","id":44392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/40920-help-the-developer-re-the-lunar-exalted?p=43464#post43464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the great poison to be Excellency prerequisites, which require you to waste your fairly limited starting Charms and bonus points to get anything even resembling breadth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that it wasn't the author's original intent to give the lunars so limited a selection of starting charms. I remember the original discussion on rpg.net but I haven't been able to find it. Here is the information from the fixalted wiki;<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://fixalted.bazzalisk.org/index.php?title=Domino%27s_Original_Chargen_Rules\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fixalted.bazzalisk.org/index.php?title=Domino%27s_Original_Chargen_Rules\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fixalted.bazzalisk.org/index.php?title=Domino%27s_Original_Chargen_Rules\" target=\"_blank\"> http://fixalted.bazzalisk.org/index.php?title=Domino%27s_Original_Chargen_Rules </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"useri